<http://example.org/flood-ontology#> rdfs:comment "An interdisciplinary flood systems ontology derived from participatory workshop knowledge graph harmonization." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1064238/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water covered Highway 96 between Center and Tenaha." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1068630/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Culverts filled with water and washed road edges on CR 532 east of Moulton." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1077070/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding occurred on numerous roadways around Victoria. This included the Navarro Street and Laurent Street Underpasses, the Five Points area, and Crestwood Drive and Ben Jordan Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1077179/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water rose above bank full on drainage ditches north of Buna flooding area roads." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1077182/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Boggy Creek exceeded bank full flooding adjacent areas near Lumberton." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1077184/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Streets were flooded and cars were stalled due to heavy rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1077778/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Strong south winds ahead of an area of low pressure forced water levels at Sabine Pass up to 4.17 feet above MLLW flooding low areas of Highway 87." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1082582/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several members of the public posted images of Padre Blvd on South Padre Island covered in one to two feet of water. One picture showed the water halfway up the wheels of a car near the Grapevine Cafe. The cause of this was the squall line that moved through early in the afternoon of April 23rd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1083255/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High northeasterly winds, associated with a wake low developing behind a thunderstorm complex, contributed to enhanced northeasterly swell which led to coastal flooding across portions of Coastal Cameron County on the afternoon of April 23rd. Water levels topped out at 2.68ft above normally dry ground around 2:30PM CDT in the Port Isabel area. Other high water levels measured included 2.32ft above normally dry ground at SPI Brazos Santiago, and 2.32ft above normally high ground at the South Padre Island Coast Guard Station. These highest levels occurred generally between 2PM CDT and 6:00PM CDT.  Several docks and a boat sustained damage from the Gale-force to Storm-force wind gusts and pounding waves associated with the event.  Dollar damages for boats are estimated and provided in a separate episode for Marine High Wind." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1083257/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High northeasterly winds, associated with a wake low developing behind a thunderstorm complex, contributed to enhanced northeasterly swell which led to coastal flooding across portions of Coastal Willacy County on the afternoon of April 23rd. Water levels topped out at 2.38ft above mean sea level (an estimated for water levels above normally dry ground) around 2:12PM CDT in the Port Mansfield area. Pictures from the Emergency Manager in Port Mansfield shows portions of docks damaged or washed away." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1084540/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media post showed Embassy Street in Las Lomas flooded with approximately 1 to 2 feet of water between E Sauz Street and Guerra Street. The worst of the flooding was near John & Olive Hinojosa Elementary School at the corner of Embassy Street and E Hinojosa Street. The flooding was caused by a thunderstorm moving slowly across southern Starr County, which produced an estimated 0.75 to 1 of rain in approximately 20 minutes. Timing based on radar estimates and the social media post." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1085010/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A portion of Highway 87-South between Center and Shelbyville was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1085011/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A portion of Southwood Drive on the south side of Lufkin was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1085012/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Tulane Drive at the Highway 287 Loop and South Medford Drive in Lufkin was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1085650/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water flooded multiple roads and vehicles across the Texas side of Texarkana." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1085651/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Highway 67 was closed at the railroad track near Lelia Street due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1088068/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law Enforcement reported Farm to Market Road 1661 and Highway 6 flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1088069/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law Enforcement reported a flooded creek and numerous roads closed in Haskell." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1088070/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was street and road flooding and vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1089015/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that U.S. Highway 75 at FM 902 was impassable due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1089018/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fire and rescue reported swift water multiple feet high and several road closures in the city of Gunter, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1089019/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that U.S. Highway 377 near the Grayson/Denton County line was impassable due to high water over the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1089028/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that floodwaters washed the top layer of asphalt off of the road near the intersection of FM 121 and Westman Road, about 2 miles west of Gunter, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092453/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that Hwy 289 at Whispering Winds was closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092454/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Randell Lake Dr was washed out due to heavy rainfall that caused the creek to rise." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092456/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The 600 block of Bois de Arc was washed out." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092736/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that fooded FM 791 at the intersection with CR 445 northeast of Campbellton." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092983/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A severe thunderstorm very slowly moved across Hale County just to the north of Plainview causing flash flooding in and around the intersection of Farm to Market Road 788 and Interstate 27." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092990/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Local broadcast media relayed reports of flooding in Parmer County along US Highway 60 between Bovina and Friona. The northbound lanes on US Highway 60 on the north side of Bovina became impassable due to flooding. Additionally, there was extensive street flooding in Friona." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1092998/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A severe thunderstorm which brought severe winds to Lubbock County also caused flash flooding around the city of Lubbock. Numerous roads in Lubbock became flooded from heavy rainfall in a short amount of time." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1093002/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous thunderstorms trained over the same area in northern Castro County early in the morning of the 27th. In addition to the training, intense rain rates led to flash flooding and many road closures. An estimated seven to nine inches of rain fell over a period of only a few hours. Farm to Market Road 1057 from Summerfield south to Farm to Market Road 2397 was closed due to flooding. Water was also covering several other roads in northern Castro County making them impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1093003/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A thunderstorm very slowly moved over central and southern Swisher County which brought heavy rainfall for several hours. Interstate 27 was closed due to flooding between Tulia and Kress." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1093106/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Members of the public shared videos of Mexico Blvd, just north of the intersection with Sam Perl Blvd, under the railroad tracks with an estimated 2 feet of water. One car was stranded and flooded in the video. The car and flooding was still there an hour later showing the car still stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1094724/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that caused street flooding near Balcones Heights." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1094726/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that caused street flooding along Salado Creek  near Hollywood Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1094728/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that caused flash flooding at I-410 and Evers Rd. and I-410 and Bandera Rd. The San Antonio Fire Department had to rescue people from cars stranded in the water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1094736/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that flooded roads in Jollyville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1094738/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that flooded the area around US Hwy 183 and Duval Rd. Approximately 30 vehicles were stranded in high water and at least 21 water rescues were performed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095526/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water was reported in the Dobbin area due to heavy rain around the intersection of Dobbin Rd and FM1486." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095527/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Both lanes of FM 2429 between SH 36 and GM 949 were closed due to floodwaters making the road impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095764/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Laredo Police Department reported flooded streets on the north side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095766/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water flooded yards due to heavy rainfall with water flowing down streets near Calallen." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095767/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency Manager reported flooding of roads along South Padre Island Drive (Highway 358) and Rodd Field Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095768/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported street flooding on the south side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095769/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported roads flooded to the northwest of Corpus Christi Naval Air Station." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1095770/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported roads flooded to the south side of Corpus Christi." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096058/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The report is from mping." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096599/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated vehicles stranded from flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096600/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated that vehicles became stranded due to flash flooding about 2 miles north northeast of Temple." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096601/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated that vehicles became stranded due to flash flooding about 3 miles north of Temple." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096705/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated street flooding 3 miles west-northwest of Temple, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096706/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A trained spotter reported street flooding about a mile east-southeast of Marlin, TX, with up to 5 inches of water on the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096709/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Amateur radio reported flash flooding near the intersection of FM 39 and FM 1512, about 9 miles northwest of Jewett, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096710/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported flash flooding in Leona." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1096713/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Texas Department of Transportation reported that FM 817 between Temple and Belton was flooded with several feet of water on it." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097019/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media reported that portions of East Central Texas Expressway at Imperial Drive in Killeen have been closed by police due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097078/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A slow moving thunderstorm produced heavy rainfall over a portion of northern Cochran County which caused flash flooding. Law enforcement reported flooding on roadways at several locations in rural Cochran County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097148/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple streets were flooded and closed across the south side of Nacogdoches. Flooding of roads were widespread across Nacogdoches County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097149/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The 3500 block of South Street in Nacogdoches was flooded and closed. A water rescue was needed for a stalled vehicle in the flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097151/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Highway 96 south of Tenaha was closed due to flooding. Numerous roads were also flooded and closed in Timpson." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097162/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiples roads were flooded throughout Central Rusk County with a few roads closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097166/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple roads remain flooded and closed across the south side of Nacogdoches due to significant flooding along Bayou La Nana. Multiple other roads were also flooded and closed throughout much of Nacogdoches County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097170/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple roads were flooded and closed through Central and Southern Panola County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097175/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The USGS Gauge on Bayou La Nana in Nacogdoches recorded a 14.3 foot rise and crested at 19.65 feet at 10 am, May 11th. This resulted in catastrophic flooding across the city of Central and Southern Nacogdoches, including the Stephen F. Austin State University campus." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097490/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous reports were received of flooded roads in the city of Lubbock and Lubbock County. Several roads were impassable and as a result were closed due to water over the roadway. Some vehicles became stranded in high waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097491/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement in Terry County reported water over the roadway on US Highway 385 between county roads 210 and 230." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097492/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A slow moving thunderstorm over southern Yoakum County created flash flooding along Texas State Highway 83 west of Denver City." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097493/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A slow moving thunderstorm moved over Motley County creating flash flooding in and around Matador. The Motley County sheriff's office reported water over the roadway on US  Highway 70/62 in Matador." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097564/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported 2 to 3 feet of water on the underpass at Highway 164 and Rusk Street in Groesbeck, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097760/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms with heavy rainfall became anchored over Lynn County during the mid-morning hours. The Texas Tech University West Texas mesonet site near O'Donnell measured 7.02 inches of rainfall. The intense rain rates and amount of rainfall resulted in the closure of a portion of US Highway 87 between O'Donnell and Tahoka. Numerous water rescues were completed and many vehicles became stranded in the flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1097761/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms that became anchored over Lynn County bringing extensive flash flooding slowly moved into central and northern Garza County spreading intense rain rates along with it. Widespread flash flooding was reported throughout central and northern Garza County. Additionally, a tractor trailer rolled over on US Highway 84 near Farm to Market Road 399 also causing a multiple vehicle wreck." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1098052/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Video evidence was sent to the forecast office in Lubbock of water rushing over Santa Fe Street east of Whiteface." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1098153/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow moving storms with intense rain rates moved over Parmer County dropping as much as one inch of rainfall in less than 20 minutes. The Friona Police Department reported that US Highway 60 in Friona was flooded. Additionally, portions of US Highway 60 outside of Friona had water over the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1098154/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The same slow moving storms that brought intense rainfall and flash flooding to Parmer County also moved over Swisher County. Similarly, the intense rainfall brought over an inch of rainfall in less than 20 minutes. The Tulia Police Department reported that several roads in town were flooded along with a few County Roads along US Highway 87." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1099613/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The road was impassable due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1099717/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A creek running through Merkel has flooded an intersection at South 11th St and Oak St." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1099720/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The public reported road flooding and vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1099721/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The report was from mping." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100211/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water was reported south of I-30 near Highway 271 near Mount Pleasant. One car was stalled in the flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100232/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Department of Transportation reported water over sections of I-14 and S W S Young Drive." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100377/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported vehicles street flooding with vehicles stranded in Aransas Pass on West Nelson Avenue and Farm to Market Road 1069." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100381/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Rockport Police Department reported several streets flooded across the city with roads impassable for small cars." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100405/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Port Lavaca Police Department reported several roads flooded across the city along with Farm to Market Road 1090. Barricades were needed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100496/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public photo of flood waters crossing FM 670 at the intersection of CR 337 in southern Mitchell County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100503/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report from mPing of street flooding, road closures, or vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100504/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Social media photos and videos show flowing water with rapids across residential roads in Big Spring. Time estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100521/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media relayed a report that Midland Fire Department was responding to cars stranded in flood waters near Loop 250 and Garfield." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100522/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media relayed a report of street flooding in Andrews. The video showed water up to the top of wheel wells on vehicles." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100524/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report from mPing of street flooding, road closures, or vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1100525/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Delayed report from mPing. Portions of Business 20 were closed due to standing water in a viaduct." .

