<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101555/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. A video on social media showed water flowing over a low water crossing on Guenther Rd. at Lane Pool Creek south of La Grange." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101587/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexar Floods reported numerous roads closed in northwestern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101588/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law Enforcement reports numerous roads and intersections under water in San Angelo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101589/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The report was from mping." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101590/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexar Floods reported water over a low water crossing on Grosenbacher Rd. north of Hwy 90." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101592/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Cars were stranded in flood water on Hwy 90 near S. General McMullen Dr. in western San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101601/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The Kirby Fire Department had to rescue people from two vehicles stranded in flood water in a low water crossing on Gibbs Sprawl Rd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101611/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Several lanes of S. Laredo St. were flooded near Apache Creek and I-35." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101613/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing FM 1447 at FM 682 southwest of Terryville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101617/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding of low water crossings on Hwy 183 north of Cuero." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101619/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported water over the road on FM 108 south of Smiley at Smith Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101620/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported FM 1353 was flooded south of Karnes City." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101622/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported water over the road on FM 766 southwest of Hochheim." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101624/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported flooded low water crossings along Hwy 119 northwest of Yorktown." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101625/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported water over the road on FM 318 northeast of Yoakum." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101626/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported water over the road on FM 532 east of Gonzales." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101629/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported low water crossings flooded on FM 237 between Yorktown and Hwy 183." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101632/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported water over the road on FM 887 west of Gillett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101634/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. TXDoT reported water over the road on FM 627 south of Gillett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101640/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing FM 3234 south of Wrightsboro." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1101667/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding in Lytle. Several roads were flooded including Benton City Rd., CR 681, and FM 2790." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102307/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Street flooding was reported in the Tomball area as a heavy downpour moved through." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102308/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Streets and yards were flooded in neighborhoods near the Hardy Toll Rd at Mesquite due to heavy rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102309/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The intersection of US-59 and Tidwell Rd was flooded by heavy rain and made impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102310/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Streets and homes were flooded across the Boca Chica Subdivision along County Road 473." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102311/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several areas were flooded across NE Harris County, including FM529 and Hwy 290, Roberts Cemetery Rd, Mesquite River Trl at Old Windmill Trl, and 249 at Killough St." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102312/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water over the roadways around Canal and 66th St made streets impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102313/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Mt. Moriah Rd Bridge was closed due to high water as a result of flooding rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102314/knowledge> rdfs:comment "N Eldridge Pkway was made impassable due to floodwaters between FM 1960 and Falbrook." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102315/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Standing water was reported on the I-69 frontage Rd near Kingwood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102665/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Black Creek rapidly rose into minor flood stage after 3 to 8 inches of rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102666/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Streets flooded after several inches of rain. One car was stalled in the intersection of Amaryllis St. and Bluebonnet Dr." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102893/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Torrential rainfall rates of 3 to 5 inches  per hour resulted in major street flooding  throughout town. Vehicles were stranded with  several water rescues being conducted. Some streets had fast  flowing water over a foot deep covering the  street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102894/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Coulter was closed at the north and south lanes at the intersection of 45th Avenue. Multiple water rescues were being conducted." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102896/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was reported to be across the road at the Canyon exit of I-27. A car had spun out and ended up in a ditch with deep water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102899/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fast moving water moved a truck bed camper at least 30 feet, and washed away several tents. As well as moved several other trailers. Flooding led to Park Road 5 being closed from the Lighthouse parking lot to the Cactus picnic area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102926/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple inches of water over rural roadways  and in yards in rural |Gray County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102932/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing the intersection of Center Point Rd. and Bear Creek Rd. in south central Gillespie County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102933/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was three feet of water over the road in the 300 block of Upper Cibolo Creek Rd. northwest of Boerne." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102934/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding causing street flooding in the Olmos Park section of San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102938/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Parkway Dr. at San Pedro Creek in northwestern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102941/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A driver encountered approximately 6 inches  of water on the roadway, causing him to  hydroplane. The swift running water carried the driver's vehicle about 80 feet from the roadway and into 3 feet of water. This person was rescued by local officials." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102946/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The low water crossing at Sleepy Hollow Dr. and Sunburst Ln. at Olmos Creek in northwestern San Antonio was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102949/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reports street flooding in Coleman." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102950/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The parking lot of Dameron Park was flooded.  Around  2 inches of rain was measured in 30 minutes by local ground observation stations." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102951/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Gordon Cummings Road was flooded due to  heavy rainfall and the overflowing of local creeks.  A water rescue did occur along this road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102954/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. A car was stranded in flood water near the St. Mary's St. bridge over the San Antonio River in downtown San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102956/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexar Floods reported several low water crossings flooded in northwestern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102958/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Local media had reported that water was getting into businesses around Hereford." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102959/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexar Floods reported flooding on Old Corpus Christi Rd. near Salado Creek in southern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1102966/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple vehicles with people inside, wound up in the ditch on US Highway 60. Reports of 6 inches of hail and 4 inches of water in the area. Water from Tierra Blanca Creek was reported to overtake the bottom of the Highway 60 bridge and start flowing over the highway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103024/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Moderate street flooding was reported throughout the city. Low water crossings in Hunsley Hills  had to be closed. Water on 4th Avenue and Hospital  Drive had stalled out smaller vehicles. ." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103059/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous reports came in for water covering roads, with fast flowing water leading to numerous roads being impassable in several areas. Drainage  ditches and playa lakes began overflowing onto  roads and encroaching on homes in the  southwest side of Amarillo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103077/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flooding. Drive Texas reported that FM 1353 was closed in both directions between Hwy 181 and FM 2102 southwest of Karnes City due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103092/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Several cars were stranded in flood water in a low water crossing at Lookout Rd. and Old O'Conner Rd. in northeastern San Antonio. A couple of people were rescued from their cars." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103095/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Several people had to be rescued from their vehicles in flood water on the I-35 frontage road at Salado Creek in southeastern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103448/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rainfall caused flooding along portions of Texas State Highway 82 and adjacent portions of CR 1115 North west of Benjamin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103449/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Significant yard flooding reported, with water nearing porches of houses. 3 to 4 inches of water was flowing over the road near the intersection of Texas State Highways 82 and 6." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103453/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Vehicles stranded near Windthorst." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1103730/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Torrential rainfall led to near zero visibilities along US Highway 84 in northeastern Hockley County as reported by local law enforcement and from public reports. Storms slowly trained over the area from central Hockley County from north of Levelland to near Anton. Water was reportedly over the roadway along US Highway 385 between Whitharral and Levelland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107181/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous road closures occurred across the city due to flash flooding.  Playa lakes were overflowing onto roads and water rescues occurred with dive  teams deployed. Several reports were relayed from  Amarillo police department and Amarillo fire  department." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107182/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple road closures occurred in Canyon due to fast  flowing water over roads. Reports were relayed  from emergency management and canyon police  department." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107185/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple reports of several roads came in for having water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107187/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Three high water rescues occurred at the US Highways 87 and 60 interchange in Canyon. Hospital Drive,  Hunsley Hills Boulevard, and Country Club  Drive were all closed as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107188/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Social  media pictures and video indicated fast moving  water flowing down a residential street.  Emergency management reported an estimated  three feet of water in some spots on the  southside of Pampa." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107191/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was occurring over the roadways of |            45th, Western and Bell Streets. Some |            locations had one to two feet of water |            across them. Water was also getting into |            yards on 45th Street. I-27 had water flowing |            down the interstate. Some water was |            threatening business on Western." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107226/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding observed near the Space Center Boulevard and Bay Area Boulevard intersection." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1107267/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Virginia Circle area was evacuated due to flooding. An estimated four feet of water  was in the parking lot of the Oakridge  Apartments as well as some commercial buildings in the area  were flooded. An estimated 130 people and 20  pets were evacuated per Amarillo Fire Department.  Multiple high water rescues were conducted by the fire department in order to evacuate residents. Multiple cars were swept away by the flood waters, ending up in ditches and submerged in water. Areas between Georgia Street and Paramount Boulevard, and from Duniven Circle area to Duncan Street were covered by standing water. Loop 335 east and westbound service road at Western as well as I-40  service road at Western were closed due to water over the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1109151/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding was reported in a lower water crossing with two high-water rescues." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1109673/knowledge> rdfs:comment "North Travis Street and U.S. Highway 75 quickly flooded due to prolonged heavy rain. The U.S. 75 service roads also flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1110120/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Widespread street and yard flooding was reported in Andrews via mPing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1110121/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media replayed a report of street flooding on the south side of Big Spring." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1112232/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law Enforcement reported Farm to Market Road 2288 at Highland Range closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1112233/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public report of flooding from mPING." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1112354/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was 2 to 3 inches of water in 3 homes on the southeast side of Merkel. Also, roads were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1112406/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Streets were briefly flooded by heavy rain in Port Neches." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1113529/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding near Lakehills." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115831/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report of flash flooding relayed from mPing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115833/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was reported over Highway 385 5 miles south of Seagraves. FM 1249 south of Seagraves is temporarily closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115836/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding report relayed from mPing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115837/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Street flooding with cars stranded was reported in Andrews. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115838/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report of flooding relayed via mPing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115839/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report of flooding relayed via mPing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1115840/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Roads were reported flooded in Big Spring. Drivers are having to turn around and detour around some roads." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1117060/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous low-water crossings flooded along US Highway 385 south of Fort Stockton." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1118016/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Reports of street flooding in the city of  Perryton were received from broadcast media.  Also it was reported that around 4 rainfall received in a short period of time." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1119703/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported damage to a fence at Wood Family Dog Park from approximately 5 inches of rushing water. Trees were also washed away at the park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1120692/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Brushy Creek overflowed Interstate 30 near FM 1565 and several cars were stuck in high water. The fast moving water swept one car off the road on the north service road and unfortunately the elderly man drowned." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1120693/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple roads were shut down in and around |            Booker. Multiple cars became stranded on |            Highway 15 west of Booker where over 2.5 |            feet of water was flowing across. County |            road D northwest of Booker and FM 377 also |            had water flowing over the road with cars |            becoming stranded. Time estimated based on |            MRMS FLASH guidance." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1123424/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Intense rain rates occurred with thunderstorm activity over central Lubbock County affecting the city of Lubbock in addition to the severe thunderstorm winds. Numerous vehicles became stalled out on the east side of the city of Lubbock. In addition, many roads were closed across Lubbock with water over the roadway. The flooding persisted well into the afternoon of the 15th as the water moved downstream into Buffalo Springs Lake and Ransom Canyon. A Texas Tech University West Texas mesonet site on the campus of Texas Tech University measured 2.43 inches of rain in 20 minutes. At least one home experienced flooding at Ransom Canyon on the south side of the lake." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1124128/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A NWS Employee reported 1 to 2 feet of flowing water just east of the intersection of Green Meadow Drive and Oak Grove Blvd. at the low water crossing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1124129/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported that the low water crossing at the Irving Street Bridge over the Concho River had several inches of fast flowing water over it." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1126332/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reports were received of high water covering the roads south of San Diego." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1126334/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report received through Facebook of 6 inches of rainfall caused flooding of roads near San Diego." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1126340/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water rescue occurred on County Road 170 north of County Road 116. Water was over the road from flooded Muerto Creek due to heavy rainfall earlier in the day." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1126341/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report received through Facebook of 6 inches of rainfall caused flooding of roads around San Diego." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1127152/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Street flooding was reported along Broadway on the East End of Galveston Island, with several cars stalled due to floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1127153/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rainfall caused floodwaters to enter an industrial building in Deer Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1127154/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rain resulted in street flooding in the Meadow Bend subdivision near FM518 in League City." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1127156/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rain from ongoing thunderstorms resulted in street flooding along NASA Boulevard in Webster." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1129969/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforceement reported water covering the road on HWY 152  near the feed lot." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1131621/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several rounds of heavy precipitation occurred from late on the first through the morning hours on the second. A number of roadways in the city of Lubbock became flooded. The heavy rain also caused the North Fork Double Mountain fork Brazos River to rise above flood stage on the southeast side of Lubbock. Farm to Market Road 835 west of Buffalo Springs Lake became inundated with flood waters and resulted in the closure of the road for a brief period on the second." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1133250/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The northwest loop exit from Interstate 37 to Highway 286 flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1133253/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding of streets occurred on 14th Street between Ailsie and Caesar Avenues in Kingsville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1133254/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The intersection of Highway 83/Interstate 35 and Mines Road was closed due to flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1133255/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rainfall flooded several intersection from the north northeast to the south southeast parts of Laredo. Highway 83 was flooded at the intersections of Market Street and Chihuahua Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1133261/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding occurred on Highway 83 at Sierra Vista Boulevard on the extreme south side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1134518/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A vehicle drove into a flooded low water crossing 5 miles north northeast of Lake Alice. The local fire department had to perform a high water rescue." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1138947/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reports (mPING) minor flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1138953/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law Enforcement reported water over Farm to Market Road 2169 near I-10." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1139204/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Four inches of rain fell in two hours leading to street flooding which caused some road closures in Booker." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1139210/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Street flooding of water around 6 deep with isolated deeper amounts was  was reported across portions of the roadways  and intersections in Perryton. There were no reports of  stalled or stuck cars." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1139211/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rains led to flooded ditches along  County Road P with water making it up  onto the rural road. Some standing water was  still on the road the next morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1139708/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report from mPING of flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1139709/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was reported across several roads in Gardendale." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1141057/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding of numerous streets and intersections occurred on the east and south side of the Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1141058/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public weather station recorded 3.66 inches in under an hour with a storm total near 4.5 inches. This caused flooding of roads on the south side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1142123/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Extensive water in flood prone areas from near Executive and Paisano Drive to Porfirio Diaz into downtown El Paso. Several stalled vehicles and water running across highways." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1142352/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rainfall in Denison caused water to flow into businesses in the downtown area. Multiple low-lying and poor drainage portions of roads were also closed in the area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1142366/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A local water level station reported water over the banks. An MPING report also indicated cars flooded near the location. A personal weather station recorded 3.62 inches of rain in one hour." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1143215/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Roadways flooded between 45th and 39th street. Few high water rescues." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144210/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water reported up to a foot deep at the intersection of Summerhill Road and Moore's Lane in Texarkana." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144211/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple roads closures and vehicles stalled in floodwaters in Texarkana, including on Kennedy Lane at Cowhorn Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144212/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Roadway flooded at the intersection of Spur 284 and FM 114 in Omaha." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144545/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing RM 189 northeast of Juno." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144546/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing RM 783 in both directions near and north of Doss." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144547/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing low water crossings along RM 648 near and east of Doss." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144548/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Several low water crossings were flooded south of Kyle including on Roland Ln. and Bunton Ln." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144549/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing streets in San Marcos near the Blanco River." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144550/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing low water crossings #50 and #51 on Cameron Rd. near Harris Branch (creek) in northeastern Austin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144551/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing low water crossings along S. Old Bastrop Hwy. south of San Marcos." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144552/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing McKie St. at Willow Springs Creek in San Marcos." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144553/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that led to flash flooding sending three feet of water over RM 335 near and downstream of the Ben Williams crossing on the Nueces River." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144581/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced locally heavy rain that sent the Llano River out of its banks. The river flooded FM 3404/Slab Rd. in Kingsland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144700/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An emergency manager reported Ranch Road 385 and Farm to Market Road 3480 was closed due to water over the road from Red Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144701/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported there was water over the road at the I-20 and US-84 split." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144702/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported flooding near South Llano River State Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144703/knowledge> rdfs:comment "NWS COOP observer reported the road to the state park is impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144704/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An emergency manager reported the road is impassable due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144705/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was flash flooding around Junction. There were road closures to County Road 450, Ranch Road 2189, County Road 410, County Road 320, County Road, Ranch Road 385 and areas along US 377. Also, there was 4 to 7 inches of rain during the past 18 hours." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144706/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was some flooding in Sonora." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144957/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple cars were stranded in flood waters on North State Highway 385 and East State Highway 83. Property cost damage is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144961/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report received from mPING of flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144962/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report received from mPING of flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1144963/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report received from mPING of flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145094/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Scurry County Emergency Manager reports Deep Creek out of its banks in Snyder leading to road closures. This flooding is a result of heavy rainfall received from last night." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145095/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was reported over the curb on Billy Hext Rd at Highway 191." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145096/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report received from mPING of flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145097/knowledge> rdfs:comment "FM 612 has flooding in multiple locations. A school bus has become stalled as a result of a low water crossing. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145113/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A trained spotter reported 1.7 inches of rain in 35 minutes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145133/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Trained spotter reported Manadas Creek overflowed into Finley Elementary School's parking lot and intersecting roads on the northwest side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145134/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported flooding of roads on the north side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145279/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Torrential rains of nearly 4 inches in an hour (2 to 3 PM CST; 3 to 4 PM CDT) fell across west Brownsville as a strong cluster of thunderstorms eased through the city. More than 3 feet of water piled up near the B&M Bridge along Mexico Blvd. near the bridge (and in the C and D street vicinity.  Several cars were submerged up to the hoods. A CoCoRaHS observer in the Los Ebanos community, 2 miles northeast of the worst flooding, recorded 3.7 inches of rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145281/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Torrential rainfall in a little more than an hour dropped between 2 and 2.7 inches of rain from east of downtown Brownsville into residential and commercial areas to the north, including known flood-prone areas along SR-4 (Boca Chica Blvd.), IH-69E frontage between Boca Chica and Morrison Blvd., and eastward to Paredes Line road.  Street flooding was most common in these areas, with water levels below 2 feet." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145289/knowledge> rdfs:comment "County Road 1676 was flooded and closed, causing a vehicle to be stranded in high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145290/knowledge> rdfs:comment "West College Avenue and South Donahoe Street were flooded in Clarksville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145291/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous roads were flooded and closed across parts of northcentral Bowie County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145292/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water reported near UT Tyler Health with several intersections flooded in the city of Tyler." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1145522/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Roads were flooded and multiple vehicles were disabled near the TX 124 and Broadway Avenue area of Winnie." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1147487/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Roma Police reported street flooding along/in the vicinity of Deer Run Avenue at approximately 4 PM CST. Time shown here allowed for a buffer based on the steady type of rain vs. convective rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1149119/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding on Blackshear Street." .

