<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197571/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Widespread heavy rainfall of three to six inches with isolated higher amounts occurred across much of the Sabine River basin of East Texas from June 2nd through June 4th, inundating the basin and especially points farther upstream and namely at Longview. As a result, the Sabine River rose rapidly into major flood stage (35 feet) late on June 10th and eventually crested near 35.9 feet on June 11th. The river remained in moderate flood stage (30 feet) through mid morning on June 19th before receding through late June." .

