<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256675/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Street and road flooding was reported via mPING in Holland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256799/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Torrential rains fell in just a few hours across Port Mansfield between 9 AM and 1230 PM CST (10 AM and 130 PM CDT), with the cooperative observer (Harbormaster) reporting 6.83 during this time.  While the town's generally decent drainage prevented a significant flood, there was minor street flooding reported in town (water of unknown depth) during the peak of the rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257154/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The intersection of FM 2493 and FM 2813 was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257165/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water covered Shiloh Road between Broadway Avenue and New Copeland Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257166/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A picture was posted to social media of flooding near businesses along Highway 110 South." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257168/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water covered South Georgia Street in Troup." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257170/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Portions of FM 747 southwest of Jacksonville were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257174/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The intersection of Canada Street and Beaumont Street in Jacksonville was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257177/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A car was stalled in high water adjacent to an insurance office along Highway 110 on the north side of Whitehouse." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257178/knowledge> rdfs:comment "FM 449 near Franklin Road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257181/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Highway 80 near Lansing Switch Road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257182/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple county roads across Harrison County were flooded and closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257260/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257263/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257266/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257267/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257270/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257274/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Late on the evening of the fifth, additional thunderstorms developed across far eastern New Mexico and moved into the extreme southwestern Texas Panhandle. These storms were oriented in a way that they trained over portions of Parmer County mostly affecting areas in and around Friona including US Highway 60 from Bovina to northeast of Friona." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257279/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Additional thunderstorms slowly moved eastward across the extreme southern Texas Panhandle from late on the fifth into the early morning hours of the sixth. An emergency manager reported water over several roads in and around Tulia including along rural roadways in Swisher County." .

