<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278156/knowledge> rdfs:comment "City of Dallas FRWS indicated that several roads were flooded and closed across northern  Dallas, including Park Central Drive at LBJ, Goforth Road at Lanshire Road, West Lawther Drive at NW Highway, and Tantor Road and Luna Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278166/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fire Department reported that two vehicles were submerged in high water near 12900 Park Central Drive at the LBJ bridge. One person was killed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278168/knowledge> rdfs:comment "San Saba Sheriff's Office reported a home near Maxwell Crossing (County Road 340) along the San Saba River was surrounded by flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278220/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported several county roads closed due to flooding and include CR 147, 120, 119, and 132." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278229/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported several road closures ENE of Cameron due to flooding. Impacted roads include CR 276, 140, 273, 250, 138, and 254." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278238/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported US-77 at Sandy Creek closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278242/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported FM 485 and FM 979 closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278246/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An EM reported CR 223, north of Cameron, was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278264/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported a water rescue on CR 941 and Sneed Creek in Freestone County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278267/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported water rescue on CR 301." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278276/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported a swift water rescue in a low water crossing near Indian trail and South Loop  Drive southeast of McGregor." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278283/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A USAF partner relayed a picture of flood waters on Elk Road (FM 2491) east of Waco." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278287/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported a swift water rescue near Waco Creek at New Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278288/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Cowhouse Creek at Pidcoke rose 16 feet in less than an hour." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278289/knowledge> rdfs:comment "South Nolan Creek and Twin Creek Rd rose 6.32 ft in less than 45 minutes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278291/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported FM 320 near Palestine closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278294/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported that both US-287 and HWY 294 near Elkhart were closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278295/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported FM 1817 near FM 2022 closed due to flooding and damage." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278296/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported road damage on FM 315 near Elmwood due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278298/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported road washed out due to flooding at CR 2608 near Tennessee Colony." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278351/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There were some locations where three to five inches of moving water accumulated on the road. Other isolated spots had one to two inches. Ditches were full in several spots and fields were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278507/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported water over the roadway at Tidwell Creek and South Main." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278509/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported that the full length of Kitty Kat Lane was closed due to flooding and is impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278514/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported East Boone Prairie Rd at Mineral Creek impassable due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278516/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported Little Mississippi Cemetery Rd impassable due to water about 1/2 mile  past the dump." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278517/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported water over the roadway at 5500 S FM 46 west of Owensville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278520/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported FM 1373 at Alligator Creek flooded and impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278521/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The EM reported the full length of Closs Rd, between Hammond and Calvert, was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278524/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The EM reported the full length of Yastic Rd, between Bremond and Hammond, was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278526/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported water over road on N FM 46 near Liere Dairy and is washed out so impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278529/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported that portions of FM 2293 between Lone Wolf Road and Walnut Creek closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278556/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding was reported on Blue Flat Road just west of the Interstate 20 Santo exit." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278559/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An EM reported 6 to 8 inches of water over the roadway at the intersection of Meixner Road and FM 308 southwest of Elm Mott." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278560/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported FM 1304 at HCR 2214 near Aquilla flooded and impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278562/knowledge> rdfs:comment "FM 933 was flooded and closed in the 1300 block south of Aquilla." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278577/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported 5 to 6 inches of water over FM 1838 south of Dawson." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278580/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported two high water rescues on the service road near mile marker 220 of Interstate 45 north of Richland. The first one was at the marked start time, and the second one was about half an hour later." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278585/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM reported a high water rescue on SW CR 2340 south of Richland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278695/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was reported over the curbs in Deep Ellum and approaching storefronts on Commerce Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278712/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A media partner relayed a report of road flooding at the Columbia Balloon base WNW of Palestine. That area had received 4.20 of rain at the time of the report." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278719/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Local law enforcement reported widespread flooding across Anderson County including 225 Spring St, FM 320, ACR 425, ACR 4251, ACR 422, ACR 4253, ACR 2202, ACR 370, and Salt Works Rd. Cars were still stalled in flood waters on 936 W Oak St. in Palestine as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278722/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing several points on Hayden Ranch Rd. west of Fredericksburg." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278723/knowledge> rdfs:comment "EM relayed a report from a trained spotter that water was over the road on LCR 456 just west of the railroad and was potentially washed out." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278734/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media reports that Main Street in Frisco between John W Elliot Drive and 2nd Street was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278749/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding sending water from Sandy Creek over RM 965 near Enchanted Rock State Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278758/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding closing FM 963 northeast of Burnet." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278762/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. The emergency manager passed a report from fire officials of a foot of water over the bridge on FM 963 over Rocky Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278770/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Cypress Creek flooded low water crossings southwest of Hunt." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278774/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Town Creek overflowed on Town Creek Rd in Kerrville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278783/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Water was a foot deep over Hwy 39 along the Guadalupe River between Hunt and Ingram." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278829/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The San Antonio Express-News reported, via video reports on social media, urban flooding with water depths up to 2 feet in streets across portions of the McAllen metropolitan region during the early to mid evening. Rainfall totals ranged from 2.5 to nearly 3 inches, much which fell within 90 to 120 minutes.  ||Damage to vehicles was unknown, though several had water levels halfway to two-thirds the way up their tire heights." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1279979/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rain resulted in flooding across northern Amarillo. Two cars were stalled at a low water crossing near Jason Avenue and  Oak Drive It appeared that water was roughly about six to eight inches deep at this location. Water also flooded the parking lot of David's Mexican restaurant on Hastings Avenue, where water depth was around six to eight inches deep." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280546/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Highway 207 in Panhandle was closed with two feet of water that accumulated under the overpass." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280564/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that caused the North Fork of the Guadalupe River to go into flood. The fire department closed RM 1340 due to water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280567/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Hwy 127 at the Frio River in Concan." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280568/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing RM 1050 at the Frio River near Garner State Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280569/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing RM 1051 at the confluence of Brushy Creek and the Dry Frio River near Reagan Wells." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280570/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing the low water crossing on CR 312 at Honey Creek southeast of Llano." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280571/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing FM 1908 at the Maverick County Canal east of Quemado." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280572/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Hwy 277 at  Quemado Creek south of Normandy." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280573/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The fire department made a high water rescue of a driver of a semi-trailer truck that was swept off Hwy 55 at the Nueces River." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280574/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Ray McDonald Ranch Rd. at the Nueces River north of Camp Wood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280575/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding sending five feet of water  from Camp Wood Creek over RR 337 northeast of Camp Wood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280576/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Montell Creek overflowed sending four feet of water over Hwy 55 south of Montell." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280580/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding.  A driver was rescued from rising floodwater at CR 416 and the Nueces River northeast of Montell." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280582/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing RM 335. The emergency manager estimated four feet of water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280585/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing several roads in county including RM 481, RM 1572, and RM 334." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280591/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. One person died at RM 187 and the Frio River when their vehicle was submerged at a low water crossing. The Frio River levels rose due to heavy rainfall upstream on the 14th and 15th." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1280782/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing FM 187 at the Sabinal River. The emergency manager reported about 1.5 feet of water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1281249/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fire Department preformed over 10 different water rescues across the Houston area.||TxDOT also reported flash flooding near I-45 and I-610. Areas west of I-45 from Telephone Rd to Roe Dr were indicated as flooded. TxDOT noted that water was covering the roadway along the westbound frontage road.||A Storm chaser also shared a video on social media, showing flooding at I-45 south and Wayside Drive. Significant inundation can be seen in the video with two cars stalled." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1281430/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Water was over roadways. Vehicle rescue and roads closed in the area of Mines Rd. and  35." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1281431/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding occurred due to heavy rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1281432/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding forced the closure of the Navarro Street underpass on Sunday, blocking  traffic at the entrances on East North Street, Navarro Street and Goodwin Avenue. City officials said barricades were placed at all entry points to keep drivers out of high water. Crews are monitoring the area and will reopen the intersection once conditions improve. Police say the intersection could remain closed until Monday." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1281955/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A report was received from the public via mPING of street/road flooding 2 miles SW of Mission Dorado. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1281995/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS employee reported a stalled vehicle in 1-2 feet of water over the road at Highway 385 (Andrews Highway) and 52nd Street in Odessa. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. The cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282302/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 2-4 inches of rain sending water from the confluence of Kent Creek and the West Frio River over RM 336 approximately ten miles north of Leakey." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282303/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 2-4 inches of rain leading to flash flooding. A video on Facebook showed the Frio River sending over five feet of water across RM 1120 south of Leakey." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282304/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 2-4 inches of rain causing flash flooding. The West Frio River sent water over Old Rocksprings Rd. south of the Happy Place Animal Rescue north of Leakey." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282307/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 2-4 inches of rain leading to flash flooding. A video on Facebook showed the Frio River sending water across RM 337 in Leakey." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282525/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several rounds of thunderstorms dropped 2-5 inches of rain causing flash flooding. The Medina River overflowed the bridge on 1st St. in Bandera." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282526/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several rounds of thunderstorms dropped 2-5 inches of rain causing flash flooding. The Medina River overflowed the bridge on Schmidtke Rd. in Bandera." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282528/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several rounds of thunderstorms dropped 2-5 inches of rain causing flash flooding. The Sabinal River flooded RM 187 at the B&R Crossing north of Utopia." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282529/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several rounds of thunderstorms dropped 2-5 inches of rain causing flash flooding. The Sabinal River flooded RM 187 at RM 337 in Vanderpool." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282532/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several rounds of thunderstorms dropped 2-5 inches of rain causing flash flooding. FM 2107 was flooded at the confluence of Rocky Creek and the North Prong Medina River northwest of Medina." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282595/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Tom Green County Sheriff's Office dispatch reported flooding along US Highway 87 near FM 2105, FM 2288, near Carlsbad and Grape Creek, where they currently have several water rescues ongoing for people trapped in flooded cars." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282609/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public photo of a home flooded with a few inches of water inside located near US Highway 87 and FM 2105." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282635/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public video of a home at the intersection of 42nd Street and Travis street with flood water inside their home as high as their knees." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282637/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public video of a home flooded on FM 2105 with at least a foot of water inside it." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282638/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public video of flooding at least two feet deep with scattered debris and water damage near 50th Street and Armstrong Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1282908/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Training thunderstorms produced around 10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the Guadalupe River in central Kerr County producing a massive flood wave that moved down river. When this flood wave reached Center Point it overtopped the San Antonio St. bridge, and the flood waters reached the intersection with Swayze St. Broadcast media video showed the water rise from its normal level to the bridge in approximately 30 minutes. When the water reached the bridge it was carrying a house that got stuck in the trees next to the bridge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283025/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The City of Brady Fire Department Rescue Team called to report that they are rescuing people out of flooded homes and people trapped in vehicles due to the flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283026/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that the town of Streeter was flooded. The time of the report was estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283027/knowledge> rdfs:comment "San Saba Sheriff County dispatch reported that there was a flooded low water crossing along County Road 362 near Dry Creek where the fire department was not able to drive through in order to respond to a house fire." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283028/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported that several homes were flooded in the City of Brady." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283029/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that most of the low water crossings and county roads across Menard County were flooded. In addition, there were several water rescues being conducted. Time is estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283030/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that US Highway 87 was flooded near Dry Prong Road, north of the city of Mason. Time was estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283031/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that there were several high water rescues including a boat rescuing people from a mobile home as well as rescuing a motorist trapped in a tree escaping the flood waters. Also, several low water crossings were flooded. Time is estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283032/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that the split at State Highway 29 and US Highway 377 was flooded, west-northwest of the city of Mason. Time was estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283033/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that a low water crossing along James River Road was flooded. Time is estimated by radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283170/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding occurred in the Bor-Ley Heights subdivision with at least one home receiving minor flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283505/knowledge> rdfs:comment "County dispatch relayed a report of multiple spots of water over the road on FM 1602 in eastern Hamilton County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283506/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Dispatch reported that FM 1602 and Hwy 22 near Lanham had water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283509/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Coryell County dispatch reported that the road was impassable due to flooding in the 6000 block of FM 217 near Turnersville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1283511/knowledge> rdfs:comment "County dispatch reported that County Road 513 near the intersection of County Road 518 south of Shive was impassible due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284029/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that FM 216 north of Iredell was closed at 10 AM due to water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284030/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that County Road 915 near the intersection of County Road 1014 northwest of Joshua was closed due to  flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284031/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media video indicated running water over County Road 906 east of Godley." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284032/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Somervell County Emergency Manager reported a vehicle stuck in high water on FM 202 southeast of Glen Rose." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284033/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that FM 56 near Brazos Point was closed due to water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284034/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fire and rescue reported 2 water rescues in Stephenville, with evacuations underway in  one neighborhood as of this report." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284035/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Comanche County Dispatch reported that County Road 434 near Proctor Lake (west of the town of Proctor) was impassible due to flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284036/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Comanche County Dispatch reported that County Road 420 was closed near Proctor Lake due to flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284037/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A news media article reported multiple roads closed in Killeen due to flooding. Streets included Stallion Drive, Tiger Lane, Woodrow Drive, Alleeta St, Bunny Trail, Tatonka Dr, Bachelor Button Blvd, Watercrest Road, and Willow Springs Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284039/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Amateur radio reported an area of impacted or closed roads due to high water between Copperas Cove and Pidcoke, including Cactus Lane at Wagon Wheel, West Avenue B from North 11th to Northern Dove Lane, and Summers Road at Ashley Drive." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284040/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management confirmed that multiple roads in Copperas Cove had become impassable due to flooding, with vehicles stranded on these roadways, primarily in residential areas on the north side of town." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1284486/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water covered Nolen Street in Kilgore." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285132/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Local broadcast media relayed a video of flooding on Interstate-27 at the Cleveland Street underpass in Hale Center. The video also showed numerous vehicles stranded in flooded waters on the Interstate Highway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285287/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS employee reported flooding in several locations along TX 349, between Lamesa and Midland. Vehicles were reported stranded in floodwaters in Lamesa. The time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. The cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285288/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Pictures of significant flooding with water covering the road on State Highway 137 just  south of Flower Grove in Martin County was shared on social media. The time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285291/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A report was received from the public of flash flooding with cars stranded on State Hwy 176 east of Grady. Pictures of the flooding were shared on social media. The time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. The cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285664/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding was shown at the Campo del Sol subdivision in northeast El Paso. In addition, media showed flooding on the Interstate 10 on ramp near downtown El Paso." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285701/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding, sand and debris on South Desert Blvd was reported at the Interstate 10 Anthony on-ramp." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285703/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding was reported in a strip mall parking lot on North Loop Drive north of Horizon Blvd with people playing in boats. Moderate street flooding was also reported along Socorro road about 2 miles northwest of Socorro." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285742/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Roads were closed around downtown El Paso near Wyoming and Kansas over to Interstate 10 near Piedras.  Roads were impassable at some places. Flash flooding also caused several walls to collapse further north near US 54 and Fort Blvd.  An apartment building in the area southwest of Fort Bliss also received flooding inside." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285811/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding was reported at Hueco Tanks State Park.  Low water crossing topped with over 6 inches of water leading into the park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1285812/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Almost 5 inches of rain was reported from multiple people in Dell City.  Roads were impassable for awhile.  Rain fell at around 1 inch per hour for 4 hours." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286010/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media report indicated flooded roads near Lindsey Drive and Jesse Drive in Copperas  Cove." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286015/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that County Road 3300 was shut down near Kempner due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286020/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that County Road 3100 just west of Brooks Crossing was shut down due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286032/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported a swift water rescue in the 1100 block of Indian Trail at a low water crossing, just southeast of McGregor." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286048/knowledge> rdfs:comment "TXDOT reported that FM 575 was closed between FM 2005 and County Road 262 northwest of Goldthwaite due to flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286067/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that County Road 218 southwest of Cameron was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286073/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that stranded motorists were extracted from flood  waters near Military Parkway and Scyene Road in Mesquite." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286074/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A trained spotter reported that flood waters were obstructing multiple lanes of Loop 12 in Irving." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286080/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media produced a video of vehicles stalled on north Dallas at West-Northwest Highway near Hillcrest due to about 6 inches of water on the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286093/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported cars stalled on Interstate 10 due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286095/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Menard County Emergency Manager reported flooding at the low water crossing at RR 865 and the San Saba River." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286096/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Menard County Emergency Manager reported that a portion of RR 1773 is closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286098/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported a flooded draw on Highway 915, north of Eldorado." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286099/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Schleicher County Sheriff's Office reported that FM 915 was closed due to flooding, approximately 3.5 miles north of Eldorado." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286100/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated that multiple vehicles were stalled on Kelly Blvd near Creekview east of Carrollton due to high water. Kelly Blvd was shut down due to it being impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286101/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that Josey Lane between Keller Springs Road and  Sherwood Lane in Carrollton was flooded by 1 foot of water, which was observed on the Josey flood gauge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286102/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that a high water rescue was conducted for a partially submerged vehicle near Addison Airport." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286103/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that a water rescue was conducted for a stranded vehicle on the Interstate 35E frontage road north of Farmers Branch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286104/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported flood waters were getting close to flooding homes on the south side of Sonora." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286105/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported 2 to 3 feet deep flood waters across RM 2291 in north-central Kimble County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286107/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Carrollton Police Department reported that the front of a westbound train was stuck in high water at the crossing at North Josey Lane and Sherwood Lane in Carrollton, which blocked Josey Lane. Traffic was backed up to Trinity Mills." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286111/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that local first responders performed a high water rescue on HWY 183 between Lampasas and Lometa, where a car was swept off the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286113/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that flooding covering US Highway 281 south of  Adamsville resulted in a temporary closure of the highway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286115/knowledge> rdfs:comment "McGregor Fire Department was dispatched to a swift water rescue at the South Bosque River crossing on Indian Trail just southeast of McGregor." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286116/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media reported that flood waters covered Oakalla Road at the Clear Creek Bridge, between Oakalla and Maxdale, causing the road to be closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286117/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that portions of FM 1851 and U.S. Highway 71 were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286120/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Mason County Sheriff's Office reported two streets significantly flooded with approximately 3 feet of water deep over the road. In addition, four low water crossings in Mason County were flooded with a foot of water deep at each of those low water crossings." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286121/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that FM 933 was closed in both directions near County Road 1221 in Blum with a water rescue needed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286122/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Menard County Emergency Manger reported that a portion of RR 1221 was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286123/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Menard County Emergency Manager reported that Ranch to Market Road 1674 in southwestern Menard County is closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286124/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that Highway 6 was closed in Iredell, and that most low water crossings across the north half of the county were closed due to flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286125/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Kimble County Emergency Manager reported that numerous roads were flooded in Kimble County, with road closures at various locations. In addition, numerous streets are flooded in Junction and Roosevelt." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286126/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that the 5700 block of FM 933 in Huron was down to 1 lane due to flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286129/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that the 1800 block along Highway 174 in Blum was closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286130/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Sutton Country Sheriff's Office reported flooding and road closures on parts of CR 864, CR 1691, CR 307, and CR 310. In addition, streets in and around Sonora are flooded as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286131/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Sutton County Emergency Manager reported that homes were being evacuated in Sonora due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286203/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reports and photos of significant flooding in the Paul Ann area of San Angelo. This included many flooded homes with water along streets 4 to 6 feet deep." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286204/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public video of a yard flooded at least a foot deep in Grape Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286205/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public video of flooding on North Bell Street, with a car stranded in flood waters. Water was up to the top of the tires of the vehicle." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286206/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public photo of flooding on Pulliam Street with at least 1 foot of water deep." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286207/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public video of a yard flooded at least waist deep." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286208/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public report of significant flooding at the Bell Street overpass along US Highway 277. The water was estimated to be at least 10 feet deep. In addition, a fire truck was fully submerged in the flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286211/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported that a large hauling trailer was displaced by the flood waters and was floating through a flooded neighborhood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286212/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported that a house was lifted off of its foundation by the flood waters and was floating down a roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286314/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fire Department reported a high water rescue at the intersection of FM 765 and County Road 450 due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286315/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported flood waters getting into homes in Menard. In addition, the flow at the San Saba River was elevated and producing flooding across a low water crossing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286325/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The McCulloch County Sheriff's Office reported widespread street flooding in the city of Brady, with several roads closed due to high flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286349/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rainfall and multiple rounds of rain brought flash flooding to north central Randall County. Vehicles were stalled in the fast moving flood waters near the US-87 and I-27 interchange. Some roads were also closed across the city of Canyon." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286350/knowledge> rdfs:comment "One to two feet of water occurred over some bridges in Palo Duro Canyon State Park with roads being closed. Campsites were evacuated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286351/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rainfall and multiple rounds of rain resulted in flash flooding across the city of Amarillo. There were multiple stalled vehicles in fast moving flood waters, especially across low lying areas in the roads, across Amarillo. Multiple roads were closed due to flash flood conditions." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286431/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported cars stalled on Interstate 10, 5 miles east of Sonora, due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286919/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS Flood Survey team found a large section of highway surface was removed by flood water on FM 1340 at Bee Caves Creek near the confluence with the North Fork Guadalupe River." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286922/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS Flood Survey team found debris along the side of FM 1340 along the North Fork Guadalupe River was eight feet above the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286929/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS Flood Survey team found debris along the side of FM 1340 at Patio Ranch Rd. W. near the confluence of Bear Creek and the North Fork Guadalupe River was ten feet above the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286933/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS Flood Survey team found large piles of debris and the guardrail destroyed at the  North Fork Guadalupe River crossing on FM 1340 just west of River Bend Rd. W." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1286934/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An NWS Flood Survey team found a section of road surface removed by flood water on FM 1340 at River Rd. just north Hunt. The highway runs parallel to the river at this point and  is 500 feet from the bank." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287369/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was catastrophic and deadly flash flooding along the South Fork Guadalupe River after around ten inches of rain fell in approximately four hours. On Hwy 39 the debris started at the confluence of Mullen Creek and South Fork Guadalupe River. The South Fork Guadalupe River topped the Hwy 39 bridge west of Auld Rd. S. and the high-water mark was 23.77 feet above the river. Five feet of water damaged the bottom floor of the River Inn and Resort. There were large sections of the exterior walls removed by water. Water reached 7.5 feet in a house along Hwy 39 which destroyed the building. Water reached the Hunt Volunteer Fire Department station on Fisher Ranch Rd. 400 feet from the river. Heart O���the Hills Camp and many houses nearby were demolished. There was major damage to Crider���s Rodeo and Dance Hall. Several homes near Hwy 39 and Rustic Hill Rd. were wiped off their foundations. The Hunt Post Office and the Hunt Store were destroyed. The first floor of a house near the confluence of the North and South Fork flooded and the residents sheltered on the second floor. Another nearby house had only one floor, and the homeowner escaped and floated on a mattress until rescued by a helicopter. Debris damaged the Hwy 39 bridge over the river in Hunt. The river gage at Hunt was destroyed, and the USGS estimated the river crested at a record 37.51 feet. Sixty-one people died in the flood along this stretch of the river, and one was still missing. Twenty-seven of the fatalities were at Camp Mystic, a summer camp for girls, including the owner of the camp, two counselors, and 25 girls ages 8-10 years old. There were 12 fatalities at the Casa Bonita neighborhood where a number of homes were washed away. Most the other fatalities were in homes along the river that were washed away. One man had helped his family escape their house through a bedroom window, but was not able to make it out himself. One person was in a vehicle trying to escape the flood water, but was washed away. Across Kerr County damage to public property and infrastructure was estimated to be $200 million. There was no damage estimate for private property. County officials estimated 2,000 structures were damaged." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287451/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was catastrophic and deadly flash flooding along the Guadalupe River after around ten inches of rain fell in approximately four hours over the headwaters of the river. The flood wave moved downstream from Hunt to Kerrville. An NWS Flood Survey team found water in some houses along the Guadalupe downstream of Hunt reached eight feet. Numerous homes were flooded in the Bumble Bee Hills subdivision. Water reached as high as 5.5 feet in houses. The Cade Loop bridge over the Guadalupe was shifted by flood water. The guardrail and roadway of the Indian Creek Rd. bridge were damaged. The guardrail was torn away as were pieces of the roadway. Two RV parks and campgrounds in Ingram were wiped away by flood water. There were 46 people killed by flood waters, and one person was still missing. All of the fatalities along this stretch of the river were in the Ingram area and most of them were from the RV parks. One man died when he severed an artery breaking a window to help his family escape their flooded house. Across Kerr County damage to public property and infrastructure was estimated to be $200 million. There was no damage estimate for private property. County officials estimated 2,000 structures were damaged or destroyed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287666/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was catastrophic and deadly flash flooding along the Guadalupe River after around ten inches of rain fell in approximately four hours over the headwaters of the river. The flood wave moved downstream from Kerrville to the Kendall County line. In Kerrville, most of the homes on Loop 13 were flooded, debris damaged the guardrail on the G St. bridge, and an apartment complex and cottages along G St. E. were damaged or destroyed by flood water. Water reached 6.5 feet inside the Center Point VFD station on Kelly St. 700 feet from the river. Ten people died in the flooding along this part of the river, and one was still missing. Most of the fatalities were people in homes that were flooded. One person was a vehicle that it is believed was swept off a bridge in Center Point. The vehicle was found a few miles downstream of the bridge. Across Kerr County damage to public property and infrastructure was estimated to be $200 million. There was no damage estimate for private property. County officials estimated 2,000 structures were damaged." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287672/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was catastrophic flash flooding along the Guadalupe River after around ten inches of rain fell in approximately four hours over the headwaters of the river. The flood wave moved downstream into Kendall County. Water from the Guadalupe backed up Cypress Creek in Comfort. Water was 5.6 feet above the bridge on 7th St in Comfort." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287689/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple rounds of thunderstorms produced 7 to 20 inches of rain over the Llano River watershed in Mason County sending a flood wave downstream into Llano County where 2-9 inches of rain fell. There was flash flooding around Castell where the Llano River overtopped the FM 2768 bridge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287690/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple rounds of thunderstorms produced 7 to 20 inches of rain over the Llano River watershed in Mason County sending a flood wave downstream into Llano County where 2-9 inches of rain fell. Flood water washed out portions of the CR 103 bridge across the river between Castell and Llano." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287702/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple rounds of thunderstorms produced 7 to 20 inches of rain over the Llano River watershed in Mason County sending a flood wave downstream into Llano County where 2-9 inches of rain fell. At Llano, floodwaters inundated portions of Badu Park and Robinson Park, with some park structures flooded at Badu Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287731/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple rounds of thunderstorms produced 7 to 20 inches of rain over the Llano River watershed in Mason County sending a flood wave downstream into Llano County where 2-9 inches of rain fell. The RR 3404 river crossing in Kingsland was overtopped. The most significant damage in Llano County was sustained to docks in the river in the Kingsland area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287862/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Flood waters inundated homes on RM 2340 near Allen Branch  Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287865/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms brought heavy rain to Burnet County for several hours. While only 1 to 2 inches of rain fell over Marble Falls, a swath of over 10 inches of rain occurred upstream in the watershed. An RV Park along Hamilton Creek in Marble Falls has at least four feet of water inundation and vehicles were floating. Residents were stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287868/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms brought heavy rain for several hours. Burnet Municipal Airport reported 8.67 inches of rain, and an LCRA gauge in Burnet reported 11.67 inches. The heavy rain flooded FM 243 and FM 1174 and made them impassable in Bertram." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287871/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the San Gabriel River in Burnet County and an additional 1-2 inches over Liberty Hill. This caused flash flooding.|Law Enforcement reported several large sheds and storage buildings moved off of their foundations and sitting along the side of Hwy 29 in Liberty Hill." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287872/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the San Gabriel River in Burnet County and an additional 1-2 inches over Liberty Hill. Liberty Hill PD reported that CR 279 is underwater, and the bridge over the South Fork San Gabriel River had several feet of water over it. Flood waters were up 15 to 20 ft high." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287877/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms produced torrential rainfall over northwestern Travis County between the late evening hours of July 4 and the early morning hours of July 5. An estimated 3 to 13 inches of rain fell within the Big Sandy Creek watershed, with the heaviest rainfall occurring in the creek headwaters near the Travis-Williamson county line. Lone Mountain Pass, north of Jonestown, was under water and impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287879/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the San Gabriel River in Burnet County and an additional 1-2 inches over Leander. There was several feet of water over the roadway on CR 267 along the South Fork San Gabriel River in Leander." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287880/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the San Gabriel River in Burnet County and an additional 1-2 inches over Leander. River Run Road was under several feet of water along the South Fork San Gabriel River in Leander." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287881/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the San Gabriel River in Burnet County and an additional 1-2 inches over Leander. Multiple houses were flooded with flowing water around them." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287883/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public reported flooding south of Brownwood near US Highway 377 and FM 1176. Parts of the road had water up the doors of an SUV." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287884/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of Cow Creek. Washouts occurred along CR 328/Cow Creek Rd. both along and over Cow Creek at multiple locations. A 66-year-old firefighter and his emergency vehicle were swept away while responding to flooding along Cow Creek near FM 1174. His vehicle was found 2 miles downstream mangled and entrenched within flood debris and sediment, but his body had not been recovered as of the time of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287886/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of Cow Creek. The FM 1431 bridge across Cow Creek was destroyed with the main bridge structure collapsing and fragmenting into at least four segments. A minivan with six occupants was swept into the creek at the crossing at around 4 AM. One of the occupants, a 17-year-old girl, was able to open the car doors and get the others to safety but died in the flooding. Her sister was also swept into the creek but survived. The Emergency Manager estimated public property and infrastructure damage at $5 million across the county. There was no estimate of private property damage." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287896/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms brought heavy rain  for several hours to Burnet on the morning of July 5. Burnet Municipal Airport reported 8.67 inches of rain. An LCRA gauge in Burnet reported 11.67 inches. The torrential rainfall caused the rapid rise of Hamilton Creek. Additional inundation also occurred along Daugherty Branch and Haynie Branch in Burnet. Homes, businesses, and other buildings along Hamilton Creek experienced up to 7 ft of inundation. Oak St. in the northwestern part of the city was especially hard hit by the swollen Hamilton Creek. Around a dozen homes along the road were damaged, primarily near 7th and 8th Street. One house was torn off its foundation and was carried by floodwaters onto the opposite side of the street. Several businesses were flooded along South Water St. A 57 year old man was swept by floodwaters while commuting through Burnet along US 281. His body was recovered about a quarter mile away from his vehicle along Hamilton Creek. Most of the units at the Hamilton Creek Manor housing complex were impacted by floodwaters. Fields at YMCA of the Highland Lakes on the south side of Burnet were damaged by flooding with fences washed out and dugouts damaged. Pafford Place Assisted Living was heavily damaged. An 85 year old man at the facility drowned in the flooding. Seven others were successfully evacuated from Pafford Place. Parts of Burnet Municipal Airport experienced 5 to 7 ft of inundation, resulting in damage to PAPI lighting and the runway. Several homes were inundated along Delaware Creek to the west and southwest of Burnet with washouts on roads. Across the county first responders rescued at least 63 people. The county Emergency Manager estimated more than 400 homes were affected and the damages were at least $6 million." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287901/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms brought heavy rain  for several hours to Burnet on the morning of July 5. Burnet Municipal Airport reported 8.67 inches of rain. An LCRA gauge in Burnet reported 11.67 inches. The torrential rainfall caused the rapid rise of Hamilton Creek. A 22 year old man commuting through Burnet was swept off the road at Park Road 4 and US 281 into Honey Creek, a tributary of Hamilton Creek. His body was recovered 8 miles downstream." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1287914/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms brought heavy rain for several hours to Burnet on the morning of July 5. Burnet Municipal Airport reported 8.67 inches of rain. An LCRA gauge in Burnet reported 11.67 inches. Floodwaters from Spring Creek impacted several mobile homes near Hwy 29 and Deer Springs Drive between Burnet and Inks Lake." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288008/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 8-10 inches of rain over the headwaters of the San Gabriel River in Burnet County and an additional 1-2 inches over Liberty Hill. First responders performed a water rescue on CR 285, southwest of Liberty Hill. Water was going through first story windows of a house." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288009/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Heavy rain from slow-moving thunderstorms fell into the Hamilton Creek watershed contributing to a rapid rise of the creek that moved downstream near Marble Falls into the Colorado River. While only 1 to 2 inches of rain fell over Marble Falls, a swath of over 10 inches of rain occurred within the watershed upstream. An LCRA stream gauge on Hamilton Creek near Marble Falls measured a rise of 18.65 ft in about 90 minutes with 49,970 cfs before the gauge stopped reporting data. Widespread inundation and downing of trees occurred along the Hamilton Creek, with the extent of inundation at times nearly 1/3 mile across near FM 1431. The CR 341 crossing along Hamilton Creek was completely washed out on both approaches, leaving only a significantly damaged central concrete segment. The south approach to the CR 340/Mormon Hill Rd crossing was scoured out by floodwaters. Several homes were flooded along Hamilton Creek Rd. farther downstream of the CR 341 crossing. The Cedar Stays RV Park, located along the creek near FM 1431, saw major impacts. About 50 RVs were parked there overnight. All RVs were impacted by flooding and most were total losses. RVs closest to the creek experienced nearly 10 ft of inundation. RVs and other vehicles were swept into trees and the surrounding vegetation. Residents awoke to water entering their vehicles and climbed atop their RVs and the roof of the RV park office to avoid floodwaters and be rescued. Helicopters and boats were dispatched to aid water rescues. A 79-year-old male resident of the park died in the flooding. Hamilton Creek floodwaters overtopped the FM 1431 bridge, damaging the guardrail and washing out part of the crossing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288010/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain while slowly moving west across Guadalupe County. Rainfall totals of 4 to 7 inches were recorded with radar estimated totals as high as 9 inches in the Seguin area. The high rain rates caused flash flooding of low-lying and poor drainage areas, leading to at least a dozen water rescues and numerous road closures throughout the city and along I-10. Rapid rises were reported along Walnut and Geronimo Creek. 3 businesses and 2 homes were flooded with 6 to 12 inches of water. The worst flooding was experienced along US-90 Alternate where widespread inundation was observed. Several city parks and recreational facilities sustained damage. Flooding caused at least $2.5 million in damage to public infrastructure." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288011/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms moved across Comal County between 8 AM and 11 AM  producing 2-6 inches of rain with the highest totals occurring along the Guadalupe River below Canyon Lake. Evacuations on River Road along the Guadalupe River began by 10 AM. At least two unoccupied RVs along River Road were swept into the river. At least a dozen low water crossings were closed west of New Braunfels, with at least three water rescues occurring in that area. On the north side of Canyon Lake, one home flooded with about 10 inches of water due to poor drainage and runoff." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288012/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Slow-moving thunderstorms produced 2-4 inches of rain in the Bulverde area. Inundation occurred at low-water crossings and other streets, including along Mustang Vista and in Oak Village North. Water rescues were reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288014/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced 2-4 inches of rain in about two hours. Flooding occurred along the intersection of US 281 and FM 1431 and damaged trails at Westside Park in Marble Falls. Several water rescues took place within the city. Several low water crossings were closed in Marble Falls. Several low water crossings were flooded in the Spicewood area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288021/knowledge> rdfs:comment "There was extensive flooding along the San Gabriel River across the county. In Georgetown two apartment complexes were evacuated. Flood waters knocked trees and damaged light poles in San Gabriel Park. Flooding at College St. and W. L. Walden Dr. prompted evacuations of the Georgetown Animal Shelter, VFW Post, Masonic Lodge, Holly Street Village, and the San Gabriel Crisis Center. The S. Austin Ave. bridge was closed. Two RV parks downstream flooded and damaged or destroyed 30 or more RVs many of which were described as unsalvageable. The city of Georgetown removed over 3500 cubic feet of debris for along the river. Across the county there were ten water rescues saving 27 people. Most of the rescues were from homes. Twenty-nine roads were closed around the county. At least six roads had damage to pavement. At least 54 structures were damaged or destroyed. The Emergency Manager estimated the cost of damage to public property and infrastructure at $25 million." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288400/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported that County Road 134 located of north of Ben Arnold was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288403/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported flooding in a home on Erin Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288407/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported a water rescue due to flooding occurred near the corner of Pulliam Street and North Baze Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288411/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported flooding in a home at 8200 North U.S. Highway 87 near Grape Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288421/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported roads inundated at and around High Street and Delphine Street in Terrell. At least one car had water up to the hood in the picture that was provided." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288425/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media video posted by KRGV-Channel 5 news showed 1 to 2 feet of water covering portions of Padre Blvd. in the City of South Padre Island, with some high water on side streets to the west, toward Laguna Madre Bay." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288427/knowledge> rdfs:comment "After a brief lull in heavy rain, another north-south oriented bands surged across already saturated ground in the Port Isabel/City of South Padre area, likely producing another round of late afternoon minor flooding with 1 to 2 feet of water covering portions of Padre Blvd. in the City of South Padre Island, with some high water on side streets to the west, toward Laguna Madre Bay.||Additional minor flooding likely occurred in poor drainage locations of Port Isabel/Laguna Heights, as total daily rainfall added up to more than 7 inches at a few locations near Laguna Heights/Laguna Vista, and more than 5 inches on South Padre Island." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288511/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Law enforcement reported flash flooding at the intersection of Coke Street and Schroeder Street which resulted in one fatality when a vehicle was swept away by the flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288637/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Numerous streets flooded on south side of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288638/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Reports of water in homes, rescues beginning. Some streets flowing like rivers." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288665/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Social media video from Facebook showed a Chevrolet pickup truck driving through several inches of standing water at the intersection of Baldwin Blvd and Osage St." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288666/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Social media post on Facebook shows photos of several inches of standing water. Photos of cars driving through the water are also included. Report came from the intersection of Baldwin Blvd, Virginia Ave, and Morgan Avenue." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1288667/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Facebook post of trash cans floating in a few inches of standing water at the intersection of Dolores St and Highland St." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1289126/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Two fatalities occurred when their SUV hydroplaned off of the US 75 service road and ended up overturned in a flooded drainage culvert. The two individuals were swept away into Post Oak Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1289514/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A delayed report was received of flash flooding between the Buffalo Trail Boy Scout Camp and State Highway 17. Roads leading into the camp were reported to be impassible, especially at low water crossings. The camp itself did not flood. The time of occurrence is  partially estimated from radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1289650/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media video shows minor street flooding along 5th Street in the community of Wichita Falls. The event time is approximate." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290134/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding was reported by the Emergency Manager which shut down Interstate 10, Executive and Paisano as well as water rescues being needed at Mesa and Mesita. A nearby Mesonet site recorded 1.8 inches in one hour." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290137/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Road closures were reported on 1st Street in Canutillo due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290138/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Broadcast media reported streets near Redd and Doniphan inundated with water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290139/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Radar estimated almost 2.5 inches of rainfall north of Fabens which created ponding of water as well as water running into structures including a restaurant in the area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290251/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that a vehicle with 2 people inside was stranded in high water on CR 3515 near CR 3510 southeast of Honey Grove." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290252/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported that several secondary roads were flooded in northern Navarro County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290417/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A broadcast media video indicated flooding on northbound I-35E near Market Center Blvd in Dallas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290418/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated that the westbound Interstate 30 frontage road was covered with one foot of water near the Erby Campbell exit." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290419/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The city of Dallas FRWS gauges indicated that Luna Road at Y Street, and Tantor Road at X Street in northwest Dallas were flooded and closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290561/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The Texas Parks and Wildlife Emergency Manager reported Dolan Creek Rd. was impassable in some spots due to flooding from Dolan Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290812/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding reported with high water covering the roadway in Joaquin near the intersection of Highway 7 and FM Road 139. Flooding was also reported just west of this location  along Highway 84 in Joaquin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290813/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding reported with high water covering the roadway on Green Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290814/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding reported with a high water rescue near Green Street and Nelson Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290815/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding reported with a high water rescue near Bill Owens Parkway at Lois Jackson Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290816/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding reported along County Road 1330, with additional flooding near the intersection of County Road 1330 and FM Road 556, and along FM Road 2254 and County Road 1342." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290817/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding reported along multiple roads across Camp County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290818/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media report indicated that Main Street at the railroad trestle, and Castle Dr between Dexham Rd and Rowlett Rd, were flooded and closed in the city of Rowlett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290819/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A City of Dallas Flooded Roadway Warning System gauge indicated that the 7400 block of Merriman Pkwy was flooded and closed along White Rock Creek in Dallas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290823/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A public report indicated that a car was stalled in flood waters near the intersection of Coit Road and Park Blvd in Plano." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290846/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. New Berlin Rd. was flooded at Woman Hollering Creek in St. Hedwig." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290847/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Ullrich Rd. was flooded at Cibolo Creek in Zuehl." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290904/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The fire department closed RM 473 at Sheps Creek west of Kendalia. There was 4.5 feet of water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290910/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood reported E. Bitters Rd. was closed at Salado Creek due to water over the road just north of San Antonio International Airport." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290917/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. A video on X showed  southbound Hwy 281 flooded near Paseo del Norte in northern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290922/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The bodies of two homeless individuals were recovered from Salado Creek near Maltsberger Ln. in northern San Antonio. Law enforcement officials believe they were swept away from a homeless encampment in a drainage channel near the creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290925/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood showed Devine Rd. closed at Olmos Creek due to water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290927/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood showed Creekview Dr. closed at Pershing Creek due to water over the road in northeastern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1290930/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood reported Blue Wing Rd. was closed due to water over the road near Salado Creek in southeastern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1292161/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several roads were flooded and closed in Rowlett including Main St at the railroad trestle, Castle Dr at Dexham Rd, and Liberty Grove at Broadmoor. Springfield Park on Hwy 66 at Antioch Dr, and Dalrock Rd at Princeton Rd were also closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1292163/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Garland PD closed Northwest Hwy at LBJ due to 2-3 feet of water on the roadway, and South 1st St at Centerville Rd and Duck Creek Dr was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1292165/knowledge> rdfs:comment "City of Dallas FWRS system reported several roads flooded and closed across northern  Dallas, including Luna Rd at Y Street, Tantor Rd at X Street, Goodnight at Walnut Hill Rd, 4201 St. Johns Drive, 7400 Merriman  Pkwy, West Lawther at NW Hwy, and the 9500 blk of Lake Highlands Rd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1292167/knowledge> rdfs:comment "US-75 northbound was closed due to flooding in a construction zone." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1292337/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Seven inches of standing water occurred in the roadway with at least one car stalled in the water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1292340/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Police blocked off the underpass on I-40 at the Ross Osage exit due to a car stranded and partially submerged in flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1293152/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Local broadcast media (KRGV Channel 5 News) provided video and still photos of street flooding in Weslaco, with 1 to 2 feet of water depth (estimated). Rainfall of 2.4 fell with a cluster of storms, including more than 2 inches in 90 minutes, at the Mid Valley Airport in Weslaco.  Similar rainfall totals were estimated in urban/poor drainage locations west to Pharr." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294169/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash Flooding was reported on multiple roadways in Snyder by the fire department. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294170/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash Flooding was reported on multiple roadways in Snyder, including at 19th and 17th Streets, Ave. O, 25th and 26th Streets, and near the water plant. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294172/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Upton County Sheriff's Office reported ongoing flash flooding near a few intersections in McCamey. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated from radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294175/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Upton County Sheriff's Office reported flash flooding along portions of State Highway 349 north of Rankin. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated from radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294177/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Reagan County Sheriff's Office reported flash flooding along a few streets in the community of Big Lake. The total time of occurrence is partially estimated from radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294206/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The Sutton County Emergency Manager reported that multiple low water crossings around the city had 1 to 3 feet of flowing water and barricades were placed at these low water  crossings." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294417/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media photo showed CR 142 flooded and impassable near Pidcoke." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294418/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A social media photo showed Bee House Creek had completely flooded CR 142 west of Pidcoke with several feet of water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294431/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Highway 207 between Conway and Claude was closed due to three feet of water over the  highway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294438/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A road northwest of Washburn was flooded with an estimated two to three feet of standing water across it.  A truck was stalled in the water and lawns and driveways had water ponded on them." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294871/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Two and half inches of rain fell in Eagle Pass, which led to flooding at the intersection of Royal Point Dr. and Royal Ridge Dr. A person was rescued from a car stranded in the flood water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294872/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Rising and fast moving water closed Roosevelt St. in Eagle Pass after 2.5 inches of rain fell." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1294875/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. One and a half to two inches of rain sent Montell Creek over Hwy 55 near Montell." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1295129/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Hueco Tanks reported 1.54 inches of rain which caused flash flooding at the state park causing the road out to be blocked and visitors stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1295136/knowledge> rdfs:comment "An mPING report of street flooding was received near McKinney." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1295137/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Rector Rd near Sanger was closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1295138/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Multiple roads were closed due to high water and include C Wolfe in Ponder, Mousehole, Jackson, and Radecke in Krum, and Swafford and Linnie Bell Rd in Justin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1295139/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Northbound I35W was been closed at Oak Street due to high water on the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1295813/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A small but potent slow-moving thunderstorm dropped rainfall rates of 2 inches per hour for about 2 hours in a small area between Olmito and Rancho Viejo, about 11 miles north-northwest of downtown Brownsville. Minor flooding of 1 to 2 feet, mainly on poor drainage roads, was observed in the area by a retired NWS employee." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297608/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Report from mping." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297741/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Moss St near downtown Gainesville and the underpass of Interstate 35 near Spring Creek were closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297742/knowledge> rdfs:comment "FM 902 near Lake Kiowa was closed due to flooding, as well as CR  174, 147, and 172 east of Gainesville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297743/knowledge> rdfs:comment "CR 224 was washed out due to floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297745/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several water rescues were conducted in the eastern part of the county including at CR 123, 150, and 175." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297746/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Highway 82 at Radio Hill Rd was closed due to flooding and could not be reopened until the following day due to the volume of water impacting the area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297747/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A water rescue was conducted near Preskitt Rd and FM 51." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297748/knowledge> rdfs:comment "The low water crossing near Whitt was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297749/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A Low water crossing near Lake Weatherford was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297750/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A low water crossing at Walnut Creek flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297751/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A vehicle was submerged in floodwaters along Interstate 30 westbound near Cherry Lane, and several other additional water rescues were reported in Fort Worth as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297752/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Vehicle stalled in floodwaters along W Vickery Blvd near Collet Park in Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297753/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several reports of high water and cars stalled on Hulen St just south of Interstate 30 in Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297754/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water reported on Norwood St south of W 7th St in Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1297755/knowledge> rdfs:comment "High water reported near the 28th St and Decatur Ave intersection north of downtown Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300259/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding with high water reported along FM Road 556 and 557 near Pittsburg." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300260/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Haverhill Drive was washed out on the southeast side of Tyler." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300261/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding with high water reported at several locations in the city of Marshall along U.S. Highway 259." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300262/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flash flooding with high water reported via social media at a residence in Melrose." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300291/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several roads were closed in north Dallas due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300292/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A stalled vehicle was reported on the Interstate 30 frontage road near Ridge Rd in Rockwall due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300293/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several road closures due to flooding were reported in Ft Worth including Pine St., Long Ave., and Park Hill. An mPING report of street flooding in north Ft Worth had been received as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300294/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A car stalled in floodwaters several feet deep near S Collard St and Tarrant Rd in Ft Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300295/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Several road closures were reported due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300296/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Flooding closed the Interstate 30 eastbound ramp to Interstate 45. High water was also reported on Interstate 35E ramps in downtown Dallas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1300633/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. RM 674 was impassable with 3-4 feet of water over the roadway north of Kickapoo Cavern State Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1301213/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency management reported significant street flooding in Menard. In addition, significant flooding was reported in the Harris Hollow section of Menard." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1301214/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency Management reported Ranch Road 2291 closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1301216/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Public posted a video was on social media, showing extensive flooding in Menard." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1301218/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Emergency Management reported water has started to enter homes in the Harris Hollow section of Menard." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1301296/knowledge> rdfs:comment "Fort Worth Alert Gauges indicated flooded roads near the 400 block of East Long Avenue and the 8000 Blk of Old Granbury Highway in northwest Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1301297/knowledge> rdfs:comment "A Fort Worth Alert Gauge indicated that the 11600 block of Oak Grove Road South was flooded in southwest Fort Worth." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#affected_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is affected by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#affects> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject produces an effect on the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#builds> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject constructs or establishes the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_built_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is constructed or established by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#comprises> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is composed of the object as a constituent part." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_part_of> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is a constituent part of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#contains_event> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject spatial concept contains the event or phenomenon of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#occurs_within> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject event or phenomenon takes place within the spatial bounds of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#controls> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject governs or regulates the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_controlled_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is governed or regulated by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#depends_on> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject requires the object for its function or existence." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_depended_on_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is required by the object for its function or existence." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#enables> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject makes possible or facilitates the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_enabled_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is made possible or facilitated by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#experience> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject undergoes or is subject to the object (typically an outcome or event)." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_experienced_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is undergone or experienced by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_attribute_of> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is an attribute or characteristic of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#has_location> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is situated at the object spatial concept." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#location_of> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject spatial concept is the location of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#has_subtype> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject has the object as a more specific subtype or subclass." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_a_type_of> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is a subclass or specific type of the object concept." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#impacts> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject has a significant effect on the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_impacted_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is significantly affected by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#includes> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject concept contains or encompasses the object concept as a part or member." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_included_in> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject concept is contained or encompassed by the object concept." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#influenced_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is affected or influenced by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#influences> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject has an effect on the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_determined_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is established or defined by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_issued_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is formally produced or released by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#issues> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject formally produces or releases the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_removed_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is eliminated or taken away by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#removes> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject eliminates or takes away the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_represented_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is represented by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#represents> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject stands for or symbolizes the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_served_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject receives service or utility from the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#serves> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject provides service or utility to the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_shaped_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject's form or structure is influenced by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#shapes> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject influences the form or structure of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_threatened_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is at risk from the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#threatens> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject poses a threat or risk to the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#is_used_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is used by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#uses> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject makes use of the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#may_be_caused_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject may be caused by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#may_cause> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject has the potential to cause the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#measured_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is measured or quantified by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#measures> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject measures or quantifies the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#validated_by> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject is validated or confirmed by the object." .

<http://example.org/flood-ontology#validates> rdfs:comment "Indicates that the subject validates or confirms the object." .

