<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1149353> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM 362 was closed near Beason Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1158440> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple ditch and stream gages indicated flooding on roadways from Beaumont to Fannett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1158441> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A stream gage on Long Branch measured water levels consistent with minor flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1158444> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Stream gages on Cow Bayou and Terry Ditch measured water levels consistent with minor flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1158447> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A water gage on Terry Gully measured water levels consistent with minor flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1158448> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The gages at the Green Acres Screw Gate and Mayhaw Bayou measured levels consistent with minor flooding from Beaumont to Fannett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159212> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing numerous low water crossings across the north and west sides of San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159215> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. A vehicle drove into flood water on Ira Lee Rd. at Corinne Dr. along Salado Creek in northeastern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159216> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding that closed the northeast entrance to the San Antonio International Airport. There was also flooding in the short-term parking garage." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159217> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. A car was submerged in fast flowing water on the Hwy 90 Frontage Road at Leon Creek in western San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159218> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. A motorist was rescued from high water on Bear Creek Pass at Bear Creek near Driftwood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159219> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that flooded FM 795 at the Liveoak Branch Creek crossing east of Gonzales." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159379> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Rising river levels into moderate stage along the Guadalupe River in combination of ongoing heavy rainfall led to a few frontage roads impassable in central to northern Victoria County according to the Texas Department of Transportation on January 24th. Flooding was most impactful during the late morning and midday hours." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159381> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Several low water crossings were closed along FM 795 and FM 532 between Gonzales and the Lavaca County line." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159384> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing a low water crossing on FM 1115 a few miles north of Waelder." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159392> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The frontage roads of Hwy 90 were closed at Leon Creek in western San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159394> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The San Antonio Fire Department had to rescue people from a car stuck in water on the I-35 N Frontage Road at Salado Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159395> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing FM 1680 southeast of Waelder." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159396> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing CR 351 at Green Dickson Park on Boggy Creek in Shiner." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159397> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing numerous low water crossing between La Grange and Round Top." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159398> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing several low water crossings in the Schulenburg area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159399> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing CR 351, CR 352, CR 344, and 6th St. near and in Shiner." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159400> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Crockett St. at N. Texana St. and CR 128/Edna St. at Rickaway Branch in Hallettsville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159401> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing FM 1116 at Salty Creek northeast of Pilgrim." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159402> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding and a high water rescue on CR 211 south of Smiley." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159403> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing numerous low water crossings between Flatonia and Schulenburg." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159404> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing numerous low water crossings in the Muldoon area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159836> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads were flooded across Harrison County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159839> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Stagecoach Road was flooded and washed out near the intersection of Pine Bluff Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159843> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A bridge on Water Street in San Augustine was closed due to flooding. Several other roads were closed from flooding in the city and throughout San Augustine County as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159844> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water rescue was reported at the intersection of Cox Road and Birmingham Road as a vehicle was washed off of the road by high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159847> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooding was reported around the Lout Town Food and Feed Store near the intersection of Texas State Highway 87 and Highway 139." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159850> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding was reported along Pershing Avenue near Chambers Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159852> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding was reported along Frank Avenue in front of Chi-St. Luke's Health Memorial Hospital." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159854> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM Road 23 just west of County Road 2214 was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1159855> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM Road 1857 just west of County Road 2213 was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1160124> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding resulted flooding along Piney Creek Road near Groveton. A man drowned in the floodwaters when attempting to retrieve items from his stranded car. Time was estimated based on radar and nearby flood reports as the man's body was not found until the next day." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1160143> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Five people were rescued from high water along FM2920 near Mueschke as a result of flooding along Spring Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1160149> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water was reported over FM 1291 at Cummins Creek as a result of excessive runoff." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1160154> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooding along the San Jacinto River resulted in extensive flooding in the McDade Estates neighborhood. Eleven adults, one infant, five dogs, and a horse were all rescued from the floodwaters. Approximately 50 homes were flooded as a result of the flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1160174> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooding along Spring Creek resulted in floodwaters covering Robert Cemetery Rd, resulting in its closure." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1162255> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 377 from Westport Parkway to Ridge Point Parkway was closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1163203> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A flooded roadway was reported along FM 905 near Jennings and Marvin communities southeast of Paris. A water rescue was conducted involving a trapped vehicle due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1163204> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooded roadway along FM 79. Water rescue of vehicle trapped by water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1164476> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain from thunderstorms resulted in flooding along Bowden Rd at Robinson Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1164477> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain from thunderstorms resulted in flooding along FM2989 at Bedias Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1165232> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain in combination of rising water levels upstream resulted in overflowing of Spring Creek covering roads and a low bridge near the corner of Raab Road and Nursery Drive. Roads appear impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1165848> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Beginning around 1700 CST to 1800 CST, severe thunderstorms began to train over eastern Stonewall County. These thunderstorms continued to back build for several hours not ending until approximately 2200 CST. Periodic rainfall rates of one to two inches per hour were estimated within this activity with a total of three to four inches of rainfall. Late in the evening, the Stonewall County sheriff's office stated that water was nearly flowing over US Highway 380 between Aspermont and Old Glory. Downstream of the reported flooding, the Double Mountain Fork Brazos River near Rule in Haskell County, Texas saw its fourth highest flow in the past four years of 2740 cubic feet per second." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1166399> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An NWS storm survey and law enforcement and public reports showed extensive flooding in rural Hall County generally along Farm to Market Road 657 between Turkey and Lakeview. Water was flowing over the roadway near the Little Red River and the Prairie Dog Town Fork Red River. Additionally, water was overflowing out of its banks along the Little Red River near Farm to Market Road 657. The rapidly flowing water knocked down vegetation, scoured the edges of the river bank, and washed out a power pole. Mud flows impacted areas north of Turkey along State Highway 70." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1166412> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An NWS storm survey revealed several flooded fields and previously flooded roadways near Farm to Market Road 193 in northwestern Crosby County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1168292> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The public reported flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1168293> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The public reported flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1171042> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 49 from the northeast side of Jefferson to County Road 248 was flooded and closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1171043> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Parts of Highway 125 southwest of McLeod were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1171044> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Parts of Highway 43 near Smithland were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173049> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported several roads closed and county roads with culverts washed out." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173050> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported road closures in the area south of Moody and a culvert collapse at Dowell Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173051> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported flooding in Mart. Water covered the yard of a resident and approached the house." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173053> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple instances of flash flooding along Highway 317 from Temple to the McLennan County line; including impassable roads and at least one vehicle stranded in high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173054> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that Highway 84 between Mexia and Teague was closed due to flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173055> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fire and rescue reported that Bushy Creek had overflowed its banks, flooding 3 or 4 homes along FM 1240. This required the evacuation of residents in the flooded homes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173057> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that numerous roads were closed between Tennessee Colony, Montalba, Elmwood, and Frankston. Creeks were overflowing and culverts were washed out." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173058> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple swift water rescues overnight in Temple including one that resulted in a fatality after a woman's vehicle was swept off the road at a low water crossing at Pepper Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173060> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported arroyos were out of their banks and stock tanks were overflowing. Also, reported 3.5 inches of rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173080> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that US 380 was closed due to flooding between Rule and FM 2407. The road was still closed on the morning of 4/28." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173571> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense portion of a line of severe thunderstorms produced heavy rainfall over southwestern Lubbock County into northern Lynn County. Numerous reports were received of water over area roadways." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173572> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense portion of a line of severe thunderstorms produced heavy rainfall over southwestern Lubbock County into northern Lynn County. Numerous reports were received of water over area roadways." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173711> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Little Pine Island Bayou near Thicket overtopped its banks flooding nearby roadways." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173713> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Deputy reports around Trout Creek indicated 4 to 5 inches of water over area roads." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173721> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Over one foot of rain occurred around the Kirbyville area in a short period of time. Several feet of flood water inundated numerous homes. The local fire department conducted several high water rescues." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173866> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a flooded roadway and parking lot at Sterrett Road and Highway 77 in Waxahachie." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173867> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media showed video of water covering neighborhood roads in Pleasant Grove." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173868> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported widespread flooding with multiple roads closed in Rowlett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173874> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Frontage roads where Nolan Creek crosses under I-35 were covered with several feet of water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173897> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Roads impassable in residential areas of Knox City due to flooding. Flooding also noted at the intersection of Texas State Highway 6 and 222. Event time is approximate." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173978> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous roads were closed due to high water across Tyler County including FM 1012, 1745, 92, 1943, and 2827 and Highways 69 and 190." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173982> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous roads were closed across Jasper County including portions of Highway 96 and FM 1747, 1004, and 777. Water was greater than 2 feet deep on Highway 96." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1173986> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highways 87 and 190 and FM 1414 closed in Newton due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174012> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several streets in Jasper were flooded with Sandy Creek at South Fletcher Street closed due to the creek making the road impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174013> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain caused South Magnolia Street south of Woodville to become impassable with other streets flooded as well. In Warren portions of FM 1420 and 1425 washed out. A church in Warren also flooded and a man had to be rescued from his property near Black Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174014> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain flooded the roadways between Silsbee and Evadale and also between Saratoga and Thicket. Mill Creek also reached major flood stage and flooded many roads and several homes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174015> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Streets and yards were flooded along FM 1130 and 1078." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174016> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several streets flooded around Nederland with a few cars flooded on South 8th Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174024> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flood waters closed Highway 96 in Kirbyville along with many other city streets. Brookshire Brothers grocery store flooded during the event with other nearby structures." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174442> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous thunderstorms grew upscale on the evening of the ninth due to several outflow boundaries. A very moist atmosphere allowed storms to produce heavy rainfall in addition to severe hail and winds. One of these storms moved over Lubbock County producing rain rates between three to five inches per hour. This caused many roads in and around the city of Lubbock to become impassable to due water over the roadway. There was a brief lull in activity between storms around 1800 CST through 2030 CST. An additional thunderstorm after 2030 CST again produced flash flooding due to heavy rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174822> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported road closures on Highway 377 near the Marshall Ridge neighborhood 3 miles south-southwest of Roanoke, TX due to high water from heavy rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174824> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that CR 4730 in Wise County became impassable due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174834> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported SH 22 was flooded east and west of Frost." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174835> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported 1 lane of Highway 175 closed at Highway 34, with high water rescues ongoing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174836> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported 8 inches of water into 4 homes in Kaufman." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174837> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Amateur radio reported water covering Highway 80 through Grand Saline, with some downtown businesses also flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174967> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Trained spotter reports completely flooded roads in Westbrook." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1174968> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "TxDOT reports dirt and debris over the roadway, water over the roadway, and low-water crossings flooded." .

