<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1175997> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING of cropland, yard, or basementflooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1175999> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 180 and FM 1269 intersection is underwater and difficult to cross." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176142> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads were reported underwater in east Odessa." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176143> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report of over-the-curb flooding of the State Highway 191 service road on the west side of Midland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176144> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "This report was received from mPING of street/road flooding, street/road closed, or vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176145> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "NWS employee reports flooding from heavy rain entering a gymnasium. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176146> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report of Loop 250 service road under water from heavy rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176147> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Photo of street flooding at the intersection of Big Spring St. and Florida Ave." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176148> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads were reported to be flooded across the Gardendale area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176156> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding was observed along State Highway 349  with multiple low water crossings impassable due to high water, especially along Independence Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176761> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported in Marshall with water covering the road at the corner of West Grand Avenue and Ward Street as well as two other nearby intersections." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176762> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads covered in high water across central and southern Harrison County, including American Plant Road, FM Road 451 near Elysian Fields High School, Blocker Road and Five Notch Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176764> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "One lane of Highway 110 North near Whitehouse closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176765> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported with high water across portions of County Road 173 near Kilgore." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176767> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Water reported to have entered a home on FM Road 9 south of FM Road 2625." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176768> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 42 near County Road 468 flooded and impassable due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176769> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported with high water covering FM Road 414." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176770> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "County Road 4530 and FM Road 2869 closed due to flooding with high water reported on numerous other road surfaces across the northern and western portions of Wood County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176771> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water reported on several county roads across the southern half of Franklin County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176772> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water reported on city streets in and around Mount Pleasant, especially on the south side of the city." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176773> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads impassable in Mount Pleasant due to very high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176774> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported in Nacogdoches via mPING." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176775> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads flooded in Nacogdoches." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1176776> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM Road 2497 near Highway 94 was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177154> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous roads across portions of the county were reported closed due Flash Flooding, including in Madisonville proper." .

