<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177164> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding in the Wolf Pen Creek in College Station resulted in nearby roadways becoming impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177165> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding along CR 247 near Midway resulted in the roadway becoming impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177169> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding resulted in widespread road closures across portions of Madison, eastern Brazos, and northern Grimes Counties." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177172> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roadways around Huntsville were closed after becoming impassable due to floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177175> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding along Hwy 287 at Bull Creek made the roadway impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177176> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple streets were flooded due to heavy rain in La Porte." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177178> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding was reported near the intersection of TX-146 and Alexander Dr in Baytown." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177179> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A section of FM 2989 was washed out by floodwaters near Falba Cemetery." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177180> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "All lanes of Hwy 59 were closed near the Baskin Loop Overpass due to flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177181> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Interstate 45 feeder road was nearly impassable due to floodwaters in the La Marque area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177182> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM 945 at the San Jacinto River was impassable due to floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177183> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooding across Huntsville State Park inundated multiple buildings with around 1ft of floodwater." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177184> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Widespread flooding was reported along multiple roadways across Mont Belvieu." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177237> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was coastal flooding (water over a bridge) near the De Zavalla Road and Elsbeth Road intersection in the Channelview area. Additionally, the Lower Todville area of Seabrook was subject to widespread coastal flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177826> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported flash flooding in Everman, where homes were flooded, roads were impassable, and some vehicles were stranded. According to local officials, the hardest hit area was homes along Christie Ave which backs up to a creek. Fourteen homes on this street had water in the homes varying up to 12 inches deep. Several of these residents were evacuated during the flooding. Local officials also reported 5 vehicle rescues during the flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177827> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A public report indicated 10 flooded roads throughout the city of Dallas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177828> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The City of Fort Worth reported several flooded roads from heavy rain: west Bonds Ranch Road, Randol Mill Rd, Waggley Robertson Road, Old Granbury Road, Golden Triangle at Alta Vista, Oak Grove Rd South, and NE 28th at Decatur Ave." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177829> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media showed video of water covering residential roads in Hillsboro and water approximately 1-2 feet deep up to home foundations. The exact location of the impacted homes is uncertain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177830> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media had video showing flash flooding of homes and residential property in the city of Kaufman due to a slow-draining nearby reservoir during heavy rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177840> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fire and rescue reported at least four roads in Temple inundated. There was also a report of one vehicle water rescue." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177841> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING: Street/road flooding; street/road closed; vehicles stranded in Holland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177842> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fire and rescue reported a vehicle almost entirely submerged at a low water crossing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177844> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a high water rescue completed at a low water crossing underpass in Groesbeck." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177845> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING: Street/road flooding; street/road closed; vehicles stranded along Hwy 164 east of Groesbeck." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177846> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple roads closed due to flooding in the city of Teague, as well as the Hwy 84 railroad underpass north of town. Many roads had at least a foot of water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1177848> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that the southbound Interstate 45 service road near mile marker 193 was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178272> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "On Suzy K St in Tarrant County, 8 total homes had water damage of varying degrees. One residence had to be evacuated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178470> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple bridges along US 84 were reported with high water, including US 84 and the Lake Mexia Bridge. Multiple areas of flooding were also reported in Mexia including a stranded motorist at HWYs 14 and 171 in Mexia." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178474> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A train derailment of 5 sand hauler cars occurred due to high water near CR 456 and CR 406." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178573> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads within the county were closed due to flooding including: FM 2728 east of Oak Ridge, CR 102, TX 243, and CR 118 near Ola, FM 2860 between Oak Grove and Becker, and CR 151 southeast of Kaufman. FM 1395 had approximately 1 foot of water flowing over the bridge, and a truck was reported as swept off the road on US 175 as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178575> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The same roadways that flooded two days prior flooded this morning as well including: FM 2728 east of Oak Ridge, CR 102, TX 243, and CR 118 near Ola, FM 2860 between Oak Grove and Becker, and CR 151 southeast of Kaufman. Minor flooding also reported across various other county roads." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178654> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple roads flooded in Mexia with one water rescue at 800 East Commerce Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1178656> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported at least 16 roads closed with some wash-outs. Five road closures isolated residents." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180165> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Pecan Bayou at Mullin rose 13 feet between 820 and 920 PM CDT." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180166> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A public report indicated a flooded home with several inches of water in the yard in Rising Star, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180169> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fire and rescue reported that TX36 was flooded and impassable at CR 414 and 412 with water rescues occurring SE of Hamilton. Flooded underpasses were also reported in Evant at US281 and US84 resulting in vehicle entrapment. Water over the bridge at CR182 was reported as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180479> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported flooded and impassable low water crossings near and north of Keene." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180480> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported numerous roads were washed out in western Bosque County. Water rescue teams unable to access an emergency scene due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180481> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Cowhouse Creek at Pidcoke rose 10 feet in 40 minutes between 140 AM and 220 AM." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180482> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A vehicle occupied by two adults and one 5 year old boy was stranded in swift water off of CR 528. A witness saw the occupants get out of the vehicle and attempt to get to dry ground on foot when all are swept into the flood waters. Responders arrived and began searching for the victims. The adults were found and rescued around 5am and transported to the hospital. The 5 year old victim was found deceased in the water around 7:20am." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180638> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Nearly two dozen roads were reported flooded across the city of Dallas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180639> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported that Trophy Club Bridge had to be closed due to flood waters, and nearby residents were notified about the flooded roads and approaching floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180640> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported a water rescue on FM 660 just north of Ennis." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180641> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple closed roads due to high water near and west of I-35 in Waco, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180642> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported a vehicle water rescue at the intersection of Shawnee Road and Bells Chapel Road, just south of Red Oak, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180647> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "TxDOT reported a road closure on Laney Street 2 miles north of Buffalo due to flooding of Buffalo Creek from heavy rainfall Wednesday night into Thursday morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180648> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a washed out culvert/road on Dowell Road near Big Elm Creek 3 miles SSE of Moody due to heavy rainfall and flooding Thursday morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180650> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a portion of Bullhide Creek Rd in McClennan County was washed out due to heavy rainfall and flooding Thursday morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180651> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported several washed out roads/culverts across Central McLennan County due to heavy rainfall and flooding Thursday morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180714> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple roadways flooded with flowing water throughout the city of Sherman." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180715> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported service roads and main lanes of I-35 closed due to flood waters several feet deep across the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1180716> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported urban flooding within the city of Groesbeck and high water near the Hwy 14 and Hwy 164 intersection." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1181301> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Miller Creek Loop Rd. south of Johnson City." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1181310> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Low water crossing #30 on McNeil Dr. in northern Austin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1181311> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that closed Cameron Rd. at Harris Branch Creek in northeastern Austin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1181862> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The public relayed a photo of standing water in a home near CR 150. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1181863> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Some roads are impassable due to flooding along W Highway 80." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182490> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Russel Creek flooded FM 1745 during a heavy thunderstorm. Roads also began to flood near Colmesneil." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182491> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Roads became flooded in Kountze and near Honey Island during heavy rain. Mill Creek also rose beyond bank full north of Silsbee." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182512> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM 2827 flooded along Kimball Creek during a heavy thunderstorm." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182513> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Black Creek overflowed flooding Highway 326." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182514> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain flooded underpasses in Beaumont. Twin City Highway flooded through Central Gardens and multiple streets also flooded in Nederland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182525> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain caused roads on the north side of Beaumont near the Parkdale Mall be be flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182527> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Woodville Fire Department reported water covering multiple streets in Woodville along with Turkey Creek flooding nearby roads. Multiple roads were also flooded near Town Bluff and Fred." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182528> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The river gage in Bevil Oaks indicated minor flooding from a thunderstorm." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182529> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Black Creek caused FM 326 to become impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182530> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads in Beaumont, Nederland, and Port Neches were closed during a slow moving line of thunderstorms including Highway 380, 347, and 366 and Nall Street. Flooding of several streets were also reported in China and Hampshire. Taylor Bayou also overflowed near Hampshire." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182531> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Cow Bayou, Cole Creek, and Terry Gully all reached moderate flood stage during a slow moving line of thunderstorms. This caused flooding of nearby areas including roads in Mauriceville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182533> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Mill Creek exceeded bank full which caused flooding of nearby streets." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1182534> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain caused multiple roads to be flooded from Warren to Colmesneil." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184084> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported multiple roadways flooded. LCR 751 in the southwest part of the county was impassable due to flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184086> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported flooding on North Carpenter between Prospect and Texas Avenue as well as flooded roadways throughout Mart." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184089> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that FM 80, south of Interstate 45, was closed due to flooding and remained closed one day later. Multiple CRs were also closed due to flooding during the heavy rain event." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184090> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple county roads closed between Jewett and Marquez due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184091> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported the Interstate 45 service road near mile marker 168 was closed due to floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184093> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several water rescues were performed in Leon Co including one on FM 542 south of Oakwood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184094> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported flooded and impassable low water crossings near Plummers Creek and LCR 456 north of Groesbeck." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184101> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported a flooded low water crossing in Groesbeck at Yeagua and Railroad. Additional flooding was reported east of Groesbeck near LCR 420 and 421 where the road was impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184102> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A public report of flooding underneath the HWY 287 bridge at Business 287 was received along with additional reports of flooded roadways west of Decatur." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184104> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported flooding on the I-35 service road south of Valley View with a vehicle water rescue." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184106> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported heavy ponding on Hwy 121 between Trenton and Westminster with multiple accidents occurring. Additional flooding was reported on the roadway at Highway 121 and 82." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184110> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported flooding over the roadway on Emberson Chapel Rd southeast of Tioga." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184112> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported an Amazon driver stalled out due to Range Creek overflowing its banks, around the 700th block of Horseshoe Road between Tioga and Collinsville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184115> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple mPING reports of flooding in Sanger were received including water over roadways." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184144> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that the 4900 block of Brushy Rd was closed due to flood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184145> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The following roads were closed in Tolar due to flash flooding: 100 W. 7th Street, 8th street behind the elementary school, and Tolar Cemetery Road at 8th Street." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184146> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported road closings on CR 1743 due to water over bridges." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184147> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported road closing on CR 1120 due to water over crossings/bridges." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184148> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported road closings on CR 1190 near Kopperl due to water over crossings/bridges." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184149> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING: Street/road flooding; Street/road closed; Vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184150> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a high water call at Interstate 14 near mile marker 290 in Nolanville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184151> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a high water call at Trimmier Rd and Lowes Blvd in Killeen." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184152> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a high water call on the 200 block of College Street in Troy." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184153> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a high water call at Shine Branch Road and SH 317 north of Temple." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184154> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING: Street/road flooding; Street/road closed; Vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184155> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING: Street/road flooding; Street/road closed; Vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184156> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Amateur radio reported that the intersection of Speeglville Rd and Hwy 84 is flooded, with picture." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184157> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Volunteer Fire Department reported water over the roadway on FM 2268 at SH 95." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184158> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Media reports all low water crossings near Salado Creek 1 mile east of I-35 are out." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184964> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The local fire department reported that an apartment complex in Rosebud was starting to flood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184965> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The local fire department reported water over the roadway on US-77 in Travis." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1184966> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fire and rescue reported water over the road on FM 413 southwest of Kosse." .

