<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185166> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several city streets in Denison were closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185168> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several county roads in southern Fannin County were closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185169> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that water flooded Highway 84 near Goldthwaite." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185172> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management reported flooded roadways in Adamsville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185173> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported several stalled cars due to flooding along portions of Legacy Drive between 121 and 75." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185174> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several county roads including 531, 612, 614, 615, 631, and 639, as well as a portion of US Hwy 84 were closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185175> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported stalled vehicles just northwest of Beverly Hills." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185177> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported roads closed just north of Beverly Hills." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185179> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported several flooded roadways in Temple." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185209> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported flooding across US 83." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185213> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported minor to moderate flooding with the depth of the water knee deep. Also, 2.90 inches of rainfall was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185216> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law Enforcement reported flooded roads between Millersview and Lake O.H. Ivie." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185221> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that 4th Street and Good Shepard Drive were covered in water and that many sections of both 3rd and Magnolia streets were also flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185225> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported US 183 from Early to the Brown/Eastland County line had been closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1185227> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported that FM 583 in Brown County had been closed due to flooding." .

