<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197514> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management reported flooding at North Catherine Street and West Alamo Dr in Terrell, TX." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197515> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple sections of Highway 2727 flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197516> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported that an SUV was found submerged in high water, and appeared to have been swept off the road from rushing water while crossing W Lawther Dr between NW Hwy and Goforth Rd. This location is just north of White Rock Lake." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197517> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that Washington St at Highway 175 in Kaufman was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197518> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported flooding along Mountain Creek Parkway. This location is just northeast of Joe Pool Lake." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1197571> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Widespread heavy rainfall of three to six inches with isolated higher amounts occurred across much of the Sabine River basin of East Texas from June 2nd through June 4th, inundating the basin and especially points farther upstream and namely at Longview. As a result, the Sabine River rose rapidly into major flood stage (35 feet) late on June 10th and eventually crested near 35.9 feet on June 11th. The river remained in moderate flood stage (30 feet) through mid morning on June 19th before receding through late June." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1199653> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Cade Loop along the Guadalupe River in Ingram." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1199654> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing RR 674 southwest of Rocksprings." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1199655> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The Kerr County Emergency Manager reported flooding along Turtle Creek west of Kerrville. There was a car stuck in high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1199656> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing several low water crossings on RR 336 north-northwest of Prade Ranch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1199657> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing several roads in eastern Bandera County including Whartons Dock Rd., Schmidtke Rd., and Lake Forest Rd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1199785> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An off-duty NWS employee and emergency manager reported flooding in southern Lynn County from heavy rainfall. Approximately six inches of water was over the roadway along US Highway 87 between O'Donnell and Tahoka." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1200425> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Minor street flooding occurred from Beaumont through Central Gardens. Stream gages also indicated bayous and ditches in the area were overflowing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1200426> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Minor street flooding occurred north of Sour Lake. A stream gage also indicated water exceeded bank full." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1200863> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Significant street flooding occurred on Stewart Rd between 81st and 75th street. Additional street flooding occurred near Moody Gardens and along Broadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1201435> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Bay Harbor area of Galveston had 16 to 18 inches of coastal flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1201437> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Water was running over Highway 87 and was bringing debris onto the roadway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202001> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Vehicle stalled due to high water with water rescue team on scene." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202470> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report of closed intersections and stalled vehicles across portions of western Midland. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202471> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Reports of multiple streets with flash flooding in northwest Midland. Flood waters are higher than sedan doors in spots. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202472> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Running water across portions of the intersection of I-20 and State Highway 158." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202479> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management reports water flowing across fields over FM 612 near Fluvanna." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202481> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management continues to report many flooded roadways around the Fluvanna area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202482> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Andrews County Emergency Management reported multiple road closures in the city of Andrews." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202483> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Curb to curb street flooding with flowing water in the Lone Star Trails Community." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202484> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "This report was received from mPING. This report indicated potential road closures." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202485> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There have been many reports of flooded roadways, stranded vehicles, and water reaching homes throughout Odessa. The cost of property damage is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202486> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was a report of flooding in north Odessa, with one vehicle stuck in flood waters. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202487> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was a report of flooding in north Odessa, with one vehicle stuck in flood waters. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202488> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The fire department reports that 41 high-water rescues were conducted around Midland over the course of the afternoon. The property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202490> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A video shows significant water over Industrial Ave. in south Midland, with at least one stranded vehicle. The property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202491> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The emergency manager reports several high-water rescues were conducted near and around Lake J.B. Thomas during the afternoon and early evening. The property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202492> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported 25 to 30 high-water rescues around Odessa during the afternoon. The cost of property damage is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202510> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "This report was received from mPING and indicated potential road closures." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202517> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "This report was received from mPING and indicated potential road closures." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202518> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooding across US Highway 84 just north of Snyder." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202519> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Video shows significant flooding across State Highway 302 near the junction with FM 1936." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202568> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report of flooding along State Highway 191 heading into Odessa. At least one vehicle is flooded. Other roads in the area are also reported to have flooding. Property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202570> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter shows a video of many water-covered roads in the Fluvanna area, primarily along FM 612 in and out of town." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202571> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "This was a report from mPING indicating potential road closures." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202572> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The photo shows one to two feet of water across an RV park in West Midland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202573> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Video of significant standing water over roads in east Odessa." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202575> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Business 20 frontage road is impassible in spots. A police cruiser is blocking the road with at least one stalled vehicle. The property damage cost is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202578> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "This was a report from mPING indicating potential road closures." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1202579> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A significant amount of water was covering FM 1298 south of Lake J.B. Thomas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1203295> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported an effort in progress helping a family out of their home which had about 2 feet of water running through it. Law enforcement also reported that E. Ranch Rd./FM 2169 is closed from Segovia to Junction." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1204425> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Local news stations reported 2 to 3 cars stranded due to high water near a construction zone on Interstate 635 and Garland Road in northeast Dallas. Two lanes were completely flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1204430> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Sherman PD reported flooding on FM 1417 on the west side of Sherman." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1204440> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flooding was reported in Sherman on Ricketts Street and Washington Street near Post Oak Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205020> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported with high watering covering Highway 2026 in Center." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205021> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported on Highway 2213 and FM Road 705 near San Augustine." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205022> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported along FM Road 2109 near Hanks Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205023> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported on FM Road 3150 near Jacks Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205024> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported on Martin Cochran Road east southeast of Huntington." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205584> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Radar estimates of 4 to 6 inches of rainfall fell over a 3 hour period. Flooding was reported with high water as high as 2 feet flowing over Highway 16 in the city of Zapata. Water was reported in a home in the Medina Addition." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205971> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Local law enforcement in Castro County reported water flowing over several roadways northwest of Dimmitt. These included Farm to Market Roads 2393 and 1055. Additionally, street flooding was reported in Dimmitt." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1205972> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A storm chaser reported water over the roadway near the intersection of Farm to Market Roads 1731 and 1760." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1206321> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported numerous road closures due to flooding over North Beach. In addition, there were several reports of water over portions of HWY-358 and in poor drainage areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1206325> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported closure due to water over roadways on FM70 from US-77 in Bishop to Chapman Ranch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1207427> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported flash flooding in portions of San Angelo in Tom Green County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1211606> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding was reported by TXDOT along Interstate 10 West near Cotton.  Gateway West was also impassable and both roads were closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212025> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Interstate 40 under the Bell Street bridge was flooded. This resulted in portions of the highway closed in both directions and water rescues also occurred at multiple underpasses." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212483> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Hwy 83 south of Catarina." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212484> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding making the intersection of Kings Way and Mary Lou Dr. in Del Rio impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212487> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing the northbound frontage road of I-35 between Randolph and Weidner in northeast San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212488> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding covering roads on the Trinity University campus. A few stranded vehicles had to be towed. The weather station on campus recorded 3.36 of rain between 6:45 AM CST and 8:15 AM CST." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212489> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding requiring several water rescues near the I-35/I-410 interchange in northeast San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212495> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The website ATXFloods.com reported several low water crossings were closed in north-central Llano County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212496> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The website ATXFloods.com reported several low water crossings flooded along Slickrock Creek in Horseshoe Bay." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1212498> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding sending water over the roadway on FM 2676 west of Rio Medina." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1215294> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rain, with measured an estimated totals of 3.5 to more than 5 inches mainly from downtown across the north and west portions of Brownsville, created numerous instances of flooding and flash flooding. Standing water was reported on the intersection of Pablo Kisel Blvd and Morrison Road. Roadway was nearly impassable. Additional reports from Cameron Co. and Brownsville Emergency Management included:  water covering roads at IH-69E Frontage and Alton Gloor, Old Alice/Barnard/Price.  A water rescue was reported downtown on 11th and Elizabeth.  Water levels in harder hit areas were between 2 and 3 feet (standing).||Damage estimates were unknown as of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216273> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was street and road flooding in Menard which resulted in roads being closed. Also, vehicles were stranded due to the high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216274> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was street flooding along Barrow street with vehicles stranded in Abilene." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216275> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Sheriffs Office reported that FM 2105 and Highway 208 was flooded north of San Angelo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216276> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported water was flowing over FM 2288 where it crossed the North Concho River." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216277> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported street flooding around Angelo State University resulting in streets being closed. Also, vehicles were were stranded. Report from mPING." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216278> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "At 735 AM CDT, the Tom Green County Sheriff Office received a call about a vehicle truck that was swept away by swift water currents in the flooded area of McMillan and Wright Roads in northeastern Tom Green County. The truck was swept approximately 150 yards from the roadway, to near a tree. The cab of the truck was submerged, and the occupants were clinging to the tree above the flood waters. All of the 5 victims were successfully rescued by first responders from the Tom Green County Sheriff Office and the San Angelo Fire Department. The Texas Department of Public Safety and Texas Parks and Wildlife Department were also involved in the rescue efforts." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216279> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A County Official reported County Road 136 is closed at the crossing over Hords Creek due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216280> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A County Official reported Farm to Market Road 1929 is closed at Fuzzy Creek due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216281> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A County Official reported the section of Arden Road is closed between Mertz road and County Road 411 due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216282> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A County Official reported Farm to Market Road 1692 is closed at the draw due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216283> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An Emergency Manager reported College Hills Blvd at Millbrook Dr is closed in San Angelo due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216284> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An Emergency Manager reported the intersection of Howard St and Webster St in San Angelo is closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216285> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An Emergency Manager reported North Archer St in San Angelo is closed at the 300 Block due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216286> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An Emergency Manager reported a section of Armstrong Street is closed between 23rd St. and 25th St. in San Angelo due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216287> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported cropland flooding. Report from mPING." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216288> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law Enforcement received a call of a fatality from flash flooding. A man was swept away by swiftly flowing water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216293> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Rain showers and thunderstorms moving out of New Mexico early on the morning of the second repeatedly trained over Parmer County producing nearly four inches of rain within a few hours. Law enforcement in Parmer County as well as pictures from social media showed water over US Highway 60 between Farwell and Bovina as well as several other roadways. Additionally, law enforcement reported several vehicles were stranded in flood waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216340> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Rain and thunderstorms grew upscale along an outflow boundary moving eastward across the South Plains. This activity trained over Lubbock County creating flash flooding across the city of Lubbock. Numerous reports were received of water over area roadways in and around the city of Lubbock. Additionally, several vehicles were stranded due to high waters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216341> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Additional thunderstorms moved over the city of Lubbock on the evening of the second. These storms produced heavy rainfall in a short amount of time across an area that already experienced flash flooding earlier in the day. These additional thunderstorms created flash flooding across the southern portion of the city of Lubbock." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216385> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The City of Fort Worth reported 3 road closures due to flooding. Two were on the south side of town (2100 blk of Cunningham St and 11600 blk of Oak Grove Rd South), and one was just north of downtown (1900 Cold Springs Rd)." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216776> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was an undetermined amount of water flowing over State Highway 4 near Boca Chica Village and the SpaceX/Starbase area during the early morning hours." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216778> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Cameron County Parks Department reported photographic evidence of 1 to 2 feet of standing water along Park Road 100 north of the City of South Padre Island during the morning of September 10th." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216903> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Roadways were flooded on Ruben M Torres Blvd near N Central Avenue with an estimated 1 to 2 feet of water depth in spots." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216911> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "San Benito PD reported various levels of flooding across town.  The following reports were received:  One foot of flowing water down Brooks Avenue at around 445 PM CDT; additional flooding on Franklin Road, Woodford Street, and Bowie Street.  Water reportedly entered homes on Bowie Street with one rescue required; water was reportedly at least knee deep in some locations (2 to 3 feet)." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216912> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Harlingen PD received numerous reports of flooded roads during the mid to late afternoon.  These included:  Fair Park Blvd, the intersection of 7th and M St, Spur 5             and Frontage, Eye St, intersection of J St and Fair Park Blvd, Bowie Ave and 25th St,             Frontage Rd. at Primera Rd exit to Wilson Rd, Le Moyne Garden, and Emerald Lake Dr. Texas Department of Transportation was notified and road closures began during the event, with water reported halfway up cars in some spots." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1216913> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rainfall, as much as 5.48 inches of rain having fallen in 90 minutes in Rancho Viejo, left pockets of flash flooding during the late afternoon between San Pedro and Olmito, including Rancho Viejo. Reports of high water into structures and vehicle rescues were reported during and after the peak of the downpour. Vehicle rescues were reported in Olmito and near Rancho Viejo; water was reportedly entering homes on Melva Court in San Pedro, and Burr Oak Loop and Agave avenue just south of IH-169 in east Olmito. ||Damage values estimated based on the reports received. || Damage information was unknown at the time of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1217429> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There were several reports of flash flooding in the city of Brownsville, mainly bracketed by Price Road and Expressway IH-69E on the west, Price Road and State Highway 48 on the east, extending to the Southmost neighborhood on the south side of the city. Reports included: Multiple intersections along Boca Chica Blvd impassable due to flooded roadways between McDavitt Blvd and  Kings Hwy and Boca Chica was nearly impassable, as well as the intersection known as Four Corners at State Highway 4; flooding extending along State Highway 4 to Southmost Blvd., and flooding along and near the frontage road at Price Road and IH-69E, extending to Barnard Road, and to nearby apartment complexes and shopping centers in this area.||While all locations inside the ascribed polygon may not have reached flash flood levels - 3 feet or higher of ponded water - the reports of impassible roads and photographic evidence suggesting pockets of this level of water depth made the case for a flash flood event in these areas.||Damage to any property was unknown as of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1217430> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Managers provided several photos of flood waters on Padre Blvd extending as far north as the intersection of Padre Blvd and Dolphin Street.  Poor drainage in the area likely contributed to water depth between 2 and 3 feet along the highway.  Damage was unknown as of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1217438> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A pocket of torrential rainfall from a nearly stationary isolated thunderstorm, with measured and estimated rainfall between 3 and 4 inches in a very small area around downtown Edinburg, left 3 feet of water in roads around the Courthouse building, some of which entered structures of estimated depths of 1 to 1.5 feet.  Damage was unknown at the time of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1217862> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Social media posts show several streets flooded in the Aransas Pass area during the morning of the 4th after nearby report rainfall totals around 8." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1217863> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "TV station KGNS stated that law enforcement in Laredo reported several streets flooded and water rescues across the city. A total of 9 children and adults were rescued from their vehicle in flooded waters. Moderate to heavy rain was falling from 10 PM CST to 5 AM CST with flooded streets persisting through the rest of the morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1217864> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A few streets remained flooded through the morning hours across the city of Laredo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1218069> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The tide levels at Sabine Pass/Texas Point reached 2.36 feet above MHHW at high tide. This caused minor flooding along Highway 82 and minor damage to an out building at Sea Rim State Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1218824> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The fire department reports a few stalled vehicles and a vehicle underwater. Property cost damage is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1218825> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several cars were stranded in high water in the city of Odessa. This report is from pictures on social media. Property cost damage is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1219112> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain in a short period of time brought flash flooding in and around the city of Brownfield late on the 17th into the early morning hours of the 18th." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1219113> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding was observed just east of Smyer along Texas State Highway 114 early in the morning of the 18th. Heavy rainfall from a line of thunderstorms produced a torrential amount of rainfall in a short period of time." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1219115> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A slow moving line of thunderstorms produced heavy rainfall over Lubbock County which caused flash flooding over the city of Lubbock. Numerous reports were received of water over area roadways. Additionally, law enforcement reported a vehicle submerged under water under the overpass of 19th street and Interstate-27." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1219117> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Runoff from heavy rainfall over the city of Lubbock early in the morning of the 18th made its way into the North Fork Double Mountain Fork Brazos River beginning on the east side of the city of Lubbock. This water eventually moved downstream into Buffalo Springs Lake. The emergency manager for Buffalo Springs Lake reported two feet of water flowing over Farm to Market Road 835 west of the lake. The emergency manager reported that the road had to be closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1221577> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Medina County 911 Dispatch received a call from an individual who was trapped in their vehicle that had been swept off Park Road 37 in high water at Mescal Creek. On the afternoon of the 5th, the vehicle was located about one mile downstream and the body of the driver 3-4 miles downstream just south of the Park Rd 37/FM 1283 intersection in Bandera County. The driver was a 20 year old male." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1221759> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management in Cameron County reported flooding in neighborhoods between Los Fresnos and Laureles due to runoff. There were reports of water depth of 3 feet in some areas. Two-day rainfall in the area ranged from 3.5 inches to nearly 6 inches." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1223218> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Marshall Drive (County Road P) was closed due to part of the road being washed out one mile east of where the pavement section of the road ends. Road P was washed out at Elk Creek. The flood was likely 200 feet wide where the road crosses Elk Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1223741> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported flash flooding at the intersection of FM 2288 and US 87 northbound." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1223744> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that a low water crossing on East Carlsbad Loop Road was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1223745> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that a home was flooded in Grape Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1223850> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple social media videos show minor roadway flooding across the central business district of the Wichita Falls community. Event time is approximate." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1223998> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing Haby Ln. and Bandera Rd. along San Geronimo Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224001> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced an estimated two to five inches of rain in three hours. This rain caused flash flooding closing Little Blanco Rd. near Twin Sisters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224002> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was a high water rescue of a vehicle stranded on Blanco Rd. at Meusebach Creek near Camp Bullis." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224005> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing roads in northwestern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224006> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain. San Antonio Fire Department rescued a person from a flooded drainage ditch near Tioga Dr. and I-10 in northwestern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224055> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Black Creek at Highway 326 reached minor flood stage. This produced minor flooding of several roadways near Black Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224056> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Water was reported over numerous roads in Lumberton. Rising water also caused multiple rescues, impassable roads, and several flooded homes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224057> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Water was reported over several roads just north of Interstate 10 near Hampshire." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224375> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported that parts of Jefferson Blvd in Cockrell Hill were impassable due to high water, and police barricades were put in place." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224376> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A mPING report indicated streets flooded and multiple vehicles stranded 2 miles north of Love Field." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224382> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A mPING report indicated streets flooded and vehicles stranded in Covington." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224755> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Water is covering the roads around Indian Point Pier. The gates have been closed to traffic. This was the case for around 2 straight weeks." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224875> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that there were roads under water north of Hords Creek Lake near Glen Cove." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224876> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that there were flooded roads near Miles." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224877> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that there were flooded roads near Fannin Elementary." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224878> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported on social media that there was flash flooding on Main Street in San Angelo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224879> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported that there was water over Irving Street in downtown San Angelo and measured 3 feet of water at a staff gage at the intersection of Avenue Q and Chadbourne." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224880> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported FM 1692 was flooded at the Willow Creek bridge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224884> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Tide levels at Sabine Pass reached 2.03 feet above MHHW at time of high tide during the evening of the 18th. This caused minor flooding of Highway 87 between Sabine Pass and Port Arthur." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224889> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Southwest of Cisco, CR 145 and CR 187 were closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224893> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Strong south winds ahead of a cold front and the remnants of Rafael in the gulf produced high tides along the coast of Jefferson County. The tide level reached 2.1 feet above MHHW which produced minor flooding of Highway 87 between Sabine Pass and Port Arthur. Minor flooding also occurred at Sea Rim State Park from high surf." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224894> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A home was reported as flooded near the Jack/Wise County line off of US Hwy 380." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224895> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A home was reported as flooded in the 2000 block of Dark Corner Road. This location is south of US Hwy 380, about half way between Bryson and Jacksboro." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224899> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Sunset VFD reported flooding on State Hwy 101 near the Big Sandy Creek Bridge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224900> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Nocona Hills VFD conducted a high water rescue on Rivercrest Drive near Lake Nocona." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1224910> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A few mPING reports of street flooding and road closures were reported in Temple." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1225045> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Sheriff's office reported flooding along the frontage road of HWY-359 and mile marker 440 from efficient rainfall rates due to a strong near stationary storm." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1226430> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Minor roadway flooding was reported by local officials." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1226431> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report indicated flooding 5 miles southwest of Springtown." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1226432> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A local official reported roadway flooding 3 miles east of Samsom Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1226435> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report indicated flooding 2 miles north of Addison." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1226815> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A stream gage reported minor flooding along Black Creek. This caused minor flooding of roads north of Sour Lake." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1226816> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A stream gage indicated water over Landis Drive southwest of Beaumont. Other locations also received minor flooding during the event with shallow water over roadways on the southside of Beaumont." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1227461> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported multiple lanes blocked on Interstate 35 East near Valwood Parkway due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1227466> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report of flash flooding was received 3 miles south of Farmer's Branch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1227468> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A social media video indicated a stalled car due to high water 2 miles west of Highland Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229328> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Rowlett Creek at both Renner Rd and Campbell Rd was reported to be rapidly rising, and a car was stranded in floodwaters on Campbell Rd due to rapidly rising water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229330> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several flooded roadway and stranded vehicle mPING reports were received from the Corsicana area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229379> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management reported several secondary roads were flooded across northern Navarro County in the Emhouse to Rice to Chatfield area as well as along the Navarro Ellis county line." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229382> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report of cropland and yard flooding was received in northern Hill County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229386> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several reports of cropland and yard flooding were reported in eastern Parker County via mPING." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229389> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report of roadway flooding and vehicles stranded was received east of Lewisville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229390> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report of a flooded roadway and/or vehicles stranded was received in the Irving area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229398> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A social media video showed widespread street flooding along Hulen St near Interstate 30 in Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1229400> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An mPING report of roadway flooding was received in Decatur." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1230373> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported water on Texas highway 87 where it meets State highway 124." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233050> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A Twitter report was received with photos of cars stalled in floodwaters on Trinity Blvd, east of Hwy 360 near the Dallas/Tarrant County line." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233051> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Facebook report of cars stalled in floodwaters along Hwy 183 on the west side of Irving." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233052> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Shawnee bridge south of Bells Chapel Rd flooded between Red Oak and Pecan Hill, and the flood gates were closed at the road to deter drivers." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233057> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads were flooded and closed across north Dallas including California Crossing, Wildwood Road, Luna Road, Tantor Road, Walnut Hill Road at Goodnight, Merriman Parkway, West Lawther at Northwest Hwy, Park Central at LBJ, and Goforth at Lanshire." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233059> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Farm to Market 71 was closed due to high water in Birthright." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233060> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A high water rescue was reported on Farm to Market Road 71 southwest of Tira." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233061> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several Farm to Market roads south of Paris were closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233062> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Royse City PD reported multiple flooded roadways in the city including FM 2642 by Verandah, Hwy 66 east of the police station, Crenshaw Road, FM 548 south of Waterscape, and Shaw Road between FM 2652 and FM 35." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233063> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A high water rescue was conducted in the 8000 blk of CR 204 between Grandview and Auburn." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233065> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads were closed due to high water near the city of Cooper including FM 1529, FM 3388, and FM 1531." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233199> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported the closure of Dunkerly Road, between Garrett and Reagor Springs, due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233200> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported the closure of Old Boyce Road, midway between Ennis and Waxahachie, due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233201> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported the closure of Mosely Road between Garrett and Reagor Springs due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233202> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a water rescue at the 900 block of Farrar Road, about 1.5 miles southeast of Rockett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233204> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported two people being swept away by flood waters and rescued on Wycliff Avenue between Oak Lawn and Highland Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233205> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that both north and south bound lanes of the Interstate 35 access roads were closed due to flooding north of Highway 77 near Red Oak." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233206> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported several roads flooded and closed in Garland including Campbell Rd at Water Oak Dr, E. Campbell Rd at Kinnertone Ln, Naaman Rd at E. Brand Rd, Naaman at E. Kingsbridge Dr, Castle Dr at Lost Pines Ln, and Castle Dr at Hickox Rd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233208> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads were flooded and closed in southern Dallas including S Harwood St, Bexar St, Illinois St, Lamar St, and Pemberton Hill." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233212> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 66 south of Highway 380 was flooded just southwest of Greenville. One vehicle was reported stranded. The report was received via social media." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233214> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous roads remain flooded and closed across the city of Dallas including S. Ervay, S. Harwood, Illinois, Lamar, Teagarden, Ravenview, 2nd Ave, Southernland, Simpson Stuart, Farragut, Hatcher, Simpson Stuart, Inwood at Park, St. Johns Drive, Easton, Ferguson, Peavy at Dixon Dr, White Rock Trail, and Park Central." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233293> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Dallas Sheriff's Office reported the I-30 eastbound service road at I-45/Highway 75 flooded and closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233294> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A Facebook report and photos showed Highway 2642 flooded north of I-30 in Royse City." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233295> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a water rescue at the 8200 block of FM 66 just south of Maypearl." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233297> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Trinity Blvd at Bear Creek became flooded in Shady Grove and was closed. A Grand Prairie alert rain gauge on the bridge measured 4.30 inches of rain in a short amount of time." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233298> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported a high water rescue at the intersection of Goforth Road and Eagle Trail in northeast Dallas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233299> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A National Weather Service employee reported several roads flooded near Hwy 360/183 area in Euless." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233300> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 1565 north of the Union Valley Fire Department and I-30 at Highway 1565 were both reported flooded per Union Valley Fire Dept on Facebook." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233301> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that US 175 and FM 148 between Kaufman and Combine were closed multiple times for flooding through early morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233302> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported that Highway 69 was closed just south of 380 due to high water on the northwest side of Greenville. One vehicle was reported stranded overnight." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233303> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a water rescue at the 5700 block of southbound I-45 service road in Garrett." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233304> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a road closure at Walker Creek Road 4 miles north-northeast of Alma." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233305> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a water rescue at the 700 block of Barton Road just northwest of Maypearl." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233306> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a road closure at JC Spence Road east of Ennis." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233307> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported a road closure at Gin Rd east of Ennis." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233308> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported that Dallas Fire Rescue boats rescued six people from a flooded home on Fireside Drive." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233309> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A National Weather Service employee reported that South Nursery Road at East Hunter Ferrell Road in Irving was impassable due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1233310> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that a car was swept off the road by high water on County Road 2065 in Horton." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1234336> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM 2118 was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1234851> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "City of Fort Worth reported a high water rescue in the 7000 blk of Trimble Drive in south Fort Worth." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1234950> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple reports of flooded roadways across Fort Worth were received including near S loop 820 and E Rosedale St." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1237988> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The left lane of I-35W southbound just north of Burleson was flooded and closed with a police barricade." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1242319> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Intense rainfall from a slow moving storm occurred in and around Happy. A Texas Tech University West Texas mesonet site near Happy measured 1.62 inches of rainfall in less than one hour. An mPing report was received of flooded roads in Happy." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1243282> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An NWS storm survey revealed significant flooding south of Crosbyton along several roadways. A slow moving supercell thunderstorm produced very heavy rainfall over an extended period of time over areas of rural Crosby County. Farm to Market 40 was covered in mud in several areas east of Texas Highway 207 indicative of water over the roadway on the night of the 24th. Most of the county roads were muddy and impassable at the time of the storm survey." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1243291> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An NWS storm survey revealed significant flooding northeast of Post along several roadways. A slow moving supercell thunderstorm produced very heavy rainfall over an extended period of time over areas of rural Garza County. Water was flowing over Farm to Market Road 2008 three miles south of Farm to Market Road 651 along McDonald Creek. Most of the county roads were muddy and impassable at the time of the storm survey." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1243293> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A slow moving supercell thunderstorm trained over areas of Motley County producing very heavy rainfall and flash flooding. An NWS cooperative weather observer reported flash flooding within the city of Roaring Springs as well as flooding over Texas State Highway 70 between Matador and Roaring Springs." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1243471> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report of street/road flooding or closures was received from mPING." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244423> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding due to heavy rain occurred over Texas State Highway 70 between Girard and Jayton. Several severe thunderstorms moved over the same area producing multiple rounds of heavy precipitation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244424> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain from severe thunderstorms repeatedly trained over central Garza County resulting in flash flooding in and around Post. Numerous streets in and around Post were inundated with water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244492> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report from mPING was received of street/road flooding or closures in Fort Stockton. Urban flooding was likely due to a slow-moving supercell thunderstorm. Time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244494> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report of street/road flooding or closures was received from mPING on the northeast side of Fort Stockton. This was likely the result of a slow-moving supercell thunderstorm. Time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244503> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report from mPING of street/road flooding or closures near I-20 was received. Time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244512> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A storm chaser reported that a large stretch of FM 2400 was under approximately 6 inches of rushing water. The entire road is flooded. Time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244513> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A part of FM 2400 was reported flooded out by at least a foot of water. A few vehicles were unable to cross the road at either end. The time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244637> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Widespread rain showers and thunderstorms developed over the South Plains region early in the morning of the sixth ahead of an upper level storm system. Moderate to heavy rain persisted for approximately two hours causing flooding of area roadways in and around the city of Lubbock. A portion of Farm to Market Road 835 was closed because it was inundated with water upstream of Buffalo Springs Lake." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244639> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Widespread rain showers and thunderstorms developed over the South Plains region early in the morning of the sixth ahead of an upper level storm system. Moderate to heavy rain persisted for approximately two hours causing flooding of area roadways in and around Sudan reported by a storm chaser. A portion of Farm to Market Road 303 was inundated with water north of Sudan." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244790> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Pecos County Emergency Manager reported approximately 4 inches of water on roads in the city of Fort Stockton, TX. Time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1244826> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report was received from mPING of street/road flooding or closures in portions of Snyder. The time is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1245011> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A nearly stationary supercell thunderstorm dropped torrential rainfall in northeastern Hockley County. A West Texas Mesonet station six miles south of Anton recorded 5.83 inches of rain, with WSR-88D MRMS rainfall estimates of six to eight inches. Numerous roads in this area were flooded and impassible for several days with vehicles reported stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1245028> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several slow moving thunderstorms trained over Hall and Childress Counties early in the morning on the 26th. WSR-88D MRMS rainfall was estimated between two to four inches over a widespread area with localized areas between four and five inches in northeastern Hall County. Numerous roads were closed or impassable in Hall and Childress Counties including US Highway 287 between Memphis and Estelline and Texas State Highway 256 between Memphis and Lakeview. One vehicle accident was reported on Texas State Highway 86 northeast of Turkey. The Prairie Dog Town Fork of the Red River filled its|banks between Estelline and Childress briefly reaching minor flood stage at the Childress 10N river gage." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1245029> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several slow moving thunderstorms trained over Hall and Childress Counties early in the morning on the 26th. WSR-88D MRMS rainfall was estimated between two to four inches over a widespread area with localized areas between four and five inches in northeastern Hall County. Numerous roads were closed or impassable in Hall and Childress Counties including US Highway 287 between Memphis and Estelline and Texas State Highway 256 between Memphis and Lakeview. One vehicle accident was reported on Texas State Highway 86 northeast of Turkey. The Prairie Dog Town Fork of the Red River filled its banks between Estelline and Childress briefly reaching minor flood stage at the Childress 10N river gage." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1245441> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency manager reported water being pumped out of a house due to flash flooding. The same emergency manager reported a stranded vehicle in east Brownsville due to flash flooding. Water levels of 2 feet or higher spread along parts of FM 511 near the Port of Brownsville, which is a typically poor-drainage location, impacting several low-wheel-base vehicles." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1245443> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rainfall with estimated totals ranging from 6 to 12 inches affected southern/southwestern Willacy County during the mid to late evening of March 27, with several water rescues reported in Sebastian along the Cameron County line.  Additional flooding with water depths on roads likely at or near 3 feet occurred northward to Lyford and perhaps the outskirts of Raymondville, and also east to FM 1420 between Santa Monica and Willamar. ||An unknown number of structures had some flooding.  Countywide damage statistics will be available later in 2025." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1245444> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rains progressed from Hidalgo into Cameron County during the evening of March 27th, with multiple repeating rounds creating rapid onset flash flooding.  The multiple rounds of rainfall in western Cameron County added up to more than 10 inches for the period, with some areas likely receiving 9 or more inches in just three hours.  Widespread flooding was reported between Santa Rosa, Combes, Palm Valley, and La Feria, with nighttime swift water rescues reported in La Feria and Santa Rosa.  The final band of torrential rain (along with strong wind) whipped through just after midnight CST (1 AM CDT) March 28th. ||The IH-2 frontage road was littered with stalled vehicles, and dozens more were removed and placed along the shoulders in each direction.  High water continued well after the rains ended, into March 29th. ||It is likely that dozens, if not over 100, structures were impacted to various degrees ranging from affected to major damage, with several likely considered destroyed. Full damage data will be available in later 2025." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1246556> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Texas Department of Transportation reported water of unknown depth was reported in an elementary school.  Photos suggested the water depth was 2 feet outside the building, and up to 1 foot inside.  Damage estimates were unknown at the time of this writing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1246558> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Two to three feet of water and flooding was reported on FM 755 in northeast Starr County near Santa Elena." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1246573> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Significant to locally devastating flash flooding began in the McAllen/Mission metropolitan area during mid-afternoon.  Rainfall rates of at least 3 in 30 minutes were too much for the city's drainage infrastructure to handle, and soon after, city fire/rescue/police reported  more than two dozen roads closed citywide and up to forty homes with an unknown amount of water depth inside, to the Emergency Management Coordinator. ||It was likely that several hundred homes had incident flooding, from affected to major damage - most concentrated in the south side of the city.  The frontage roads on IH2 (Mission/McAllen) and IH-69C (Pharr/Edinburg) flooded with varying amounts of water, and hundreds of vehicles were stranded.  The highest water was at least four feet in spots along the frontage south of the McAllen Convention Center. Rainfall rates were historic for the season, ranging from 1/100 to 1/200 probability events (annual return frequency) over a 2-hour period. McAllen/Miller Airport, located just south of IH-2 and just west of 10th Street, recorded 6.25 in two hours.  ||Additional reports of 2 to 3 feet of water were received from the City of Pharr, with two to three feet of water depth at the intersection of N. Cage Blvd. and E. Ferguson Ave., along/near the IH-69C frontage.  Additional, faster moving/impacting rain bands occurred during the late evening, with the final potent band (with wind) racing through just after 11 PM CST (midnight CDT March 28th).  Residual urban flooding and high water would continue into March 28th and beyond in some areas.||As of early July, a county-wide estimate of Public Assistance (PA) and Individual Assistance (IA) damage was $52 million in Hidalgo County. The data were applied to this entry, since the combination of heavy rainfall and infrastructure was highest in this area at this time. More accurate damage reports for the City, and Hidalgo County overall, will be provided toward the end of 2025 or early 2026." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1247310> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Video of notable street flooding in El Cenizo, time estimated from video author." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1247388> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Media reported street flooding at the intersection of Airline Rd and McArdle Rd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1247389> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Off duty NWS employee shows photos significant street flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1248430> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported 2 to 3 inches of water on side roads." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1249502> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency manager reported a closed road due to urban flooding in Palm Valley near the intersection of Queens Sago Dr and Stuart Place Rd.  Time of event estimated by radar and duration of estimated rainfall of 3 to 4 inches in two hours." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1249529> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING of Cropland/Yard Flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1249908> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rains moved out from the McAllen/metro into the mid-Valley section of Hidalgo County, to include locations east of Edinburg, including Elsa/Edcouch, then south through San Juan, Alamo, and Donna, extending south to around Military Highway (US 281) east of Pharr and near the Rio Grande.||Poor drainage locations flooded with at least 3 feet of water depth, and nearly the entire IH-2 frontage road had 2 to 3 or more feet of water depth, with dozens of vehicles stranded and at least one hundred more removed from the floodwaters. A number of farm-to-market and state highways had pockets of flood waters, forcing closures that lasted into March 28th. ||In this flood area, there were three known drownings when vehicles became submerged in deeper waters in canals/drainage areas during encounters with law enforcement.  One drowning was a juvenile who was unable to be rescued from a vehicle that submerged near Edcouch.||Damage details and further information will be available later in 2025 from these areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1249922> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rains that previously affected the McAllen/Edinburg metro area reached southeast Hidalgo County, from south of Weslaco to Edcouch and east to the Hidalgo/Cameron line, then south along the Mercedes/La Feria line and all the way to between Progreso and just west of Santa Maria. Similar to the situation in the Donna-Weslaco area, the IH-2 frontage road was littered with flooded vehicles, with rescued vehicles along the side of the elevated expressway.  An estimated 3 or more feet of water was on the frontage roads.||The rain in this area came in multiple rounds.  A first round occurred between 430 and 6 PM, with additional rounds between 7 and 8 PM and again fro 930 to around 11 PM,and a final windy round around midnight March 28th CST (1 AM CDT). Water rescues were first reported in Mercedes at around 7 PM CST (8 PM CDT).  As of this writing, damage was unknown but hundreds of structures likely had varying degrees, ranging from affected to major damage.   ||High water would continue well into March 28th and beyond; the flood control system (floodway) had up to 20% capacity due to spillage and pumping of urban flood areas into it. ||Full damage statistics will be available later in 2025." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1249939> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Some of the heaviest rainfall associated with the historic rainfall of March 26-28 fell in Harlingen.  In total, nearly 19 inches was measured by trusted sources, with radar estimates up to 20.5 inches.  During the peak of the multiple bands from early evening through just after midnight on the 28th, estimated rainfall rates were at least 3 per hour for at least 3 hours, including at Harlingen/Valley International Airport, where 5 fell in just 90 minutes before the power went out due to lightning strikes.||Hundreds, if not a thousand, structures had flood damage ranging from affected to destroyed. Damage details will be available for this part of Cameron County, which stretches from Harlingen through Rio Hondo and southwest to San Benito, at a later date in 2025.  Harder hit areas reported up to 4 feet of water, including the IH-2 and IH-69E frontage roads in these areas. For several areas, this event ranked as a 1/100 to 1/200 annual return frequency probability event, with perhaps up to a 1/500 event in a few spots. High water would continue in several hours for a few more days, though rapid runoff allowed for relatively quick recovery.||As of July 1, a preliminary estimate of $105 million was derived from Public Assistance (PA) and Individual Assistance (IA) reports, based on applying two-thirds of the values from the number of structures that were impacted with varying levels of damage in Cameron County. The damage was applied to this entry, since much was triggered by the rainfall and rainfall rates in these areas at these times. Full damage statistics will be available by the end of 2025 or start of 2026." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1250287> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Texas Department of Transportation, along with local law enforcement and the public, noted a continuation of high water along the IH-2 frontage roads between Mission and Alamo from just before midnight (standard time) on March 27th through mid to late afternoon on the 28th, as water was slow but steady to drain out of the area despite fair weather for most of the period." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1250288> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Texas Department of Transportation, along with local law enforcement, the public, and emergency management, reported high standing water of 2 to 3 feet in several poor drainage locations of southeastern Hidalgo County that persisted for two more days following historic seasonal rainfall/rainfall rates.  ||This included much of the IH-2 frontage road from east Alamo through the Cameron County line (Mercedes/La Feria), as well as several Farm-to-Market roads which remained impassible for all or part of this time. Overwhelmed drainage systems took time for the water to run out completely, and the Flood Control Project (Main and North Floodways in southeastern Hidalgo County between Weslaco and Mercedes, extending north to La Villa and east to the Willacy County line near Santa Rosa) continued with up to an estimated 20% of freeboard (capacity).||An unknown number of homes in southeast Hidalgo County had at least 1 foot in them, especially in the poorest draining locations where at least 10 inches of rain fell on the 27th into very early on the 28th. ||Damage estimates will be included with the initial flash flood entries from March 27th." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1250289> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Texas Department of Transportation, along with Cameron County and local city emergency management between La Feria and Rio Hondo, and other law enforcement, and neighborhood groups reported a continuation of 2 to 3 feet of water depth (higher in a few locations) well into March 28th, with only a slow recession on the 29th and 30th before the water drained out for all but a few locations. Flood related impacts continued as follows:||*Much of the IH-2 frontage between La Feria and Harlingen, and the IH-69E frontage from the Willacy County line through San Benito, was under 2 to 3 feet of water.|*The Arroyo Colorado gauge in Harlingen recorded a record high level of 30.44 feet at 7 AM on March 28th. While some of the record water levels were due to slow flows due to a need for dredging of sediment and other debris, locations inside the levee saw water levels greater than those seen from all but Hurricane Beulah, and low water crossings in western Cameron County were under at least 2-3 feet of water depth.|*State and Farm-to-Market roads between Harlingen and Rio Hondo remained closed from at least 2 feet of water depth well into the 28th.  |*Numerous homes, vehicles, and more remained under water in Palmview, Combes, Rio Hondo, Harlingen, and Primera.  The community of Green Valley was especially hard hit.  |*The duration of high water was partly driven by drainage backups and fill-ups in the Flood Control project of canals, ditches, and conveyance through-ways between Hidalgo, Cameron, and Willacy - with northern Cameron County communities bearing the brunt due to their location having the heaviest rainfall totals, which extended into southeast Hidalgo County. ||Water finally drained out except for a few locations by March 30th.  Final damage statistics will be included in the Flash Flood entry that includes the Harlingen/Rio Hondo/San Benito area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1250292> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Texas Department of Transportation continued to report flooding along the frontage road near Sebastian well into March 28th, with additional flooding noted by emergency management/law enforcement along Farm-to-Market and County roads in the southern portion of the county.  Flooding continued at homes in the Sebastian area where drainage backups remained.||There was an unknown amount of water remaining in the North Floodway of the International Boundary and Water Commission's Flood Control Project.  Further details for Willacy County flooding well after the rains ended will be provided through updates." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1251158> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding north of Uvalde. The Uvalde Fire Department rescued a person from high water at Hwy 83 and CR 429 along Leona Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1251159> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding north of Uvalde. The Uvalde Fire Department rescued a person from high water on Puccini Ln along the Taylor Slough in Uvalde." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1253530> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "There was a report of road flooding along state route 163." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1253536> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public report of a creek overflowing." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1253541> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported flash flooding across streets with a few vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1253543> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported a creek overflowing due to flash flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1253544> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public report of street flooding due to flash flooding and a few vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1253545> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported road flooding due to flash flooding and a few vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1254186> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Slow moving and repeated rounds of thunderstorms in and around Old Glory brought an extended period of heavy rainfall. A report from mPing indicated water over the roadway along US Highway 380." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1254187> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Two supercell thunderstorms merged south of Roaring Springs near Texas State Highway 70. The combined supercell remained nearly stationary over this area for approximately 30 minutes consistently dropping very heavy rainfall before moving eastward. After the initial supercell thunderstorm moved east, additional thunderstorm development upstream moved over the same area bringing further heavy rainfall. The heavy rain mostly affected the Roaring Springs Ranch Club. Water was reported over the roadway along Texas State Highway 70 at the South Pease River (Tongue River) intersection. There was an unknown amount of damage reported within the ranch club as well as water over the highway." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1254188> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads were flooded and closed around Warren including 1943 East and West, CR 4475, FM 1013  CR 4478. Multiple other roads had water covering them, but were not closed including CR 4470 and CR 1450." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1254246> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Many dry creeks had fast flowing water in them along Texas Highway 70 between Brice  and Clarendon." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255083> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A portion of FM-174, just west of the Brock Road intersection, was impassable due to flooding. Event time is approximate." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255509> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous streets flooded throughout the City of Victoria." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255510> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous sites at Riviera Beach Trailer Park are flooding due to heavy rain." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255511> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Roads are starting to flood throughout the area." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255790> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Bryan PD reported multiple streets and intersections flooded including: Villa Maria at Harvey Mitchell; Palasota at Finfeather; 500 West Carson; 200 block of Dodge; North Coulter at Park Street; Briarcrest at Earl Rudder Frontage; Carter Creek near Tanglewood Park. Broadcast media also reported flooded roadways in the Braeburn cul-de-sac near Broadmoor Drive in Bryan, TX near Briar Meadows Creek. A member of the public also reported inundation on South College Avenue at Inflow Blvd in central College Station. Inflow Blvd borders a ditch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255792> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A member of the public reported flash flooding with water inundating Greens Prairie Road at Royder Road just south of College Station." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255827> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "At least four to five inches of flowing water occurred across the intersection of FM2391 and County Line Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255830> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rainfall resulted in up to eight inches of standing water along 23rd and 25th avenues on the north side of Pampa." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255896> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The city of Bowie Police Department closed Nelson Street at Mill Street, Nelson Street at the railroad bridge, and Decatur Street due to flash flooding. Social media video also indicated several flooded roads throughout the city of Bowie." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255908> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Amateur radio passed along reports of water coming into homes, water over roadways, and stranded cars in Nocona. The Montague County Sheriff's Office also reported that US Highway 82 was closed in both directions in Nocona." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255911> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple high-water rescues in the northern part of Montague County. Multiple boat crews were requested to assist." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255913> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A public report indicated that US-81 north of Stoneburg remained closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255914> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported multiple county roads and bridges washed out across the county. Flooding was still ongoing, and Highway 81 near Nocona remained closed due to flooding as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255917> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several mPing reports for flooding were received across Collin County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255918> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several mPing reports for flooding were received across Dallas County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255919> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Portions of Old Granbury Rd in southwest Fort Worth were reported closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255934> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A mPing report for flooding was received from the city of Cooper." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255939> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported several county road closures near Cooper including the following: FM 2068, FM 128, FM 1529, and FM 71. State Highway 24 North on the southbound lanes was also closed due to flooding on the low bridge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255940> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Social media reports indicate several roads flooded in and around Paris, including Highway 195 and 24th Street. A few homes were also flooded as well as some vehicles." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255941> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A social media video indicated approximately 6 inches of water covering the road just north of the city of Graham, with 8 to 12 inches in one spot." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255942> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Social media photos and videos showed several roads flooded across Corsicana." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255944> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported several roads flooded across the city of Bowie." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255945> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several roads were flooded across Montague County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255946> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported flooding on Rosamond Pkwy east of Hwy 75 in the city of Anna." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255951> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Amateur radio reported street flooding across Bridgeport and a tree blocking the road on FM 2123 near the Bridgeport Golf Course. Amateur radio also specifically reported Hovey Street and 10th street was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255953> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported street flooding in Savoy and Bells, with Hwy 56 at the railroad bridge on the Grayson/Fannin County line closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255954> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Amateur radio reported flooding near the intersection of FM 1810 and CR 1340 east of the city of Chico." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255956> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported 7 roads flooded and closed across Denton, including the I-35 exit at University Drive, Mingo Road underneath Loop 288, and Blagg Road from Mayhill Street to Geesling Road. Other roads flooded and closed across Denton County included Fritz Lane in Corinth, South Shady Shores Road from Parkside Lane to Montserrat Road in Lake Dallas, Liberty Road near McNatt Road in Aubrey, and Creek Hill Way from 12th Street to Hardeman Circle in Justin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255957> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported that floodwaters as high as car headlights covered parking lots and roads in the city of Krum." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1255974> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The 2900 block of Keller Hicks Rd near Haslet was reported to be closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256011> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The 1200 block of NE 28th Street in Fort Worth (near the Stockyards) was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256205> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A road closure was reported near Coit Rd and Lewis Canyon Dr in Prosper." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256207> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flood waters covered Inwood Rd between Loop 12 and I-635." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256211> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Many road closures were reported in Jack County due to flooding. Impacted areas included Burwick Rd between Highway 380 and FM 1191, FM 4 one mile south of Jacksboro, and Rock Creek Rd two miles east of FM 1191." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256213> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fort Worth Fire Department responded to six high water rescues across the city." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256226> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple flooded roads were reported in Wise County, including portions of W Thompson St, FM 51, Old Decatur Rd at Alvord Rd, Halsell St, and several county roads." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256230> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A road closure was reported near Highway 78 and Century Way in Wylie due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256255> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads were closed in Fort Worth due to flooding, including portions of E Long Ave, Alta Vista Rd, and Trinity Blvd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256260> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Dallas PD responded to a high water rescue at Shady Trail and Glenda Ln. Dallas Fire Rescue reported 13 high water rescue calls across the city." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256262> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple stalled cars and one high water rescue was reported due to flooding on Saginaw Blvd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256265> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Street flooding was reported in Granbury." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256290> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A creek overflowed resulting in water moving into a yard and basement of a home near Mineola." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256311> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple creeks overflowed their banks near Lindale." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256351> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Pictures were posted to social media of significant street flooding in Lindale." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256353> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "South Texas Street was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256354> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered Highway 37 just south of Bogata." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256356> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered portions of Highway 49 in low lying areas. A local tow operator estimated water 6-8 feet deep in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256358> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered multiple roads in Gilmer." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256364> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding throughout the Texas side of Texarkana. High water covered Exit 220 on I-30 West." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256365> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered Main Street and other side streets in Atlanta." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256366> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered Lake Placid Road in Tyler." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256368> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered portions of I-30 on the Texas side of Texarkana. Stateline Avenue was also flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256370> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Interstate 30 was shut down from Mile Marker 220 to the Arkansas state line due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256372> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Rushing water covered CR 2041 just south of Appleby." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256374> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple creeks overflowed their banks near Mount Vernon." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256530> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported high water on TX Highway 31 west of Corsicana. The road was becoming impassable in spots." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256533> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The 5100 block of Erath Street in Forest Hill/southeast Fort Worth was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256535> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fire and rescue reported water over Highway 84 East in Fairfield. Several side streets were also flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256537> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported significant flooding in a Fairfield neighborhood with at 1-2 feet of water running across yards and streets." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256538> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Anderson County Emergency Management reported flooding of low lying areas across the county with 4.55 inches of rain measured in Tennessee Colony." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256540> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that Luella Road at the Choctaw Creek bridge, about midway between Luella and Sherman, was flooded by one foot of water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256541> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that multiple streets in Bridgeport were flooded. Pioneer Road in New Fairview was also closed due to high water.." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256542> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported a home flooded on Dynasty Drive in Glenn Heights." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256543> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported that McKinney Street at Ennis Avenue was flooded, and a car was stalled in flood waters on Ennis Avenue at Clay Street in the city of Ennis." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256660> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A car was stranded and a high water rescue was conducted at Highway 14 and CR 244 north of Mexia." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256665> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Sachse Rd at Muddy Creek between the cities of Sachse and Wylie was closed due to high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256671> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A water rescue was reported at 412 CR 941, located west of Fairfield." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256675> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Street and road flooding was reported via mPING in Holland." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1256799> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Torrential rains fell in just a few hours across Port Mansfield between 9 AM and 1230 PM CST (10 AM and 130 PM CDT), with the cooperative observer (Harbormaster) reporting 6.83 during this time.  While the town's generally decent drainage prevented a significant flood, there was minor street flooding reported in town (water of unknown depth) during the peak of the rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257154> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The intersection of FM 2493 and FM 2813 was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257165> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered Shiloh Road between Broadway Avenue and New Copeland Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257166> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A picture was posted to social media of flooding near businesses along Highway 110 South." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257168> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered South Georgia Street in Troup." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257170> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Portions of FM 747 southwest of Jacksonville were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257174> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The intersection of Canada Street and Beaumont Street in Jacksonville was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257177> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A car was stalled in high water adjacent to an insurance office along Highway 110 on the north side of Whitehouse." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257178> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM 449 near Franklin Road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257181> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 80 near Lansing Switch Road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257182> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple county roads across Harrison County were flooded and closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257260> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257263> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257266> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257267> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257270> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An intense and long-lived supercell thunderstorm slowly tracked to the east across portions of Hockley, Lamb, Hale, Lubbock, and Crosby Counties. In addition to producing very large hail and numerous tornadoes, it also created very heavy rainfall which led to flash flooding across a large area of the South Plains. Several reports were received from storm chasers across Hockley, Lamb, and Hale Counties of water over many roadways. Numerous reports from Lubbock County and area web cams showed water flowing over city streets as deep as three feet in some areas." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257274> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Late on the evening of the fifth, additional thunderstorms developed across far eastern New Mexico and moved into the extreme southwestern Texas Panhandle. These storms were oriented in a way that they trained over portions of Parmer County mostly affecting areas in and around Friona including US Highway 60 from Bovina to northeast of Friona." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257279> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Additional thunderstorms slowly moved eastward across the extreme southern Texas Panhandle from late on the fifth into the early morning hours of the sixth. An emergency manager reported water over several roads in and around Tulia including along rural roadways in Swisher County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257519> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Portions of South Georgia Street in Troup was covered in high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257520> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Portions of FM 747 southwest of Jacksonville was covered in high water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257522> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The intersection of Canada and Beaumont Streets in Jacksonville was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257523> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 80 near Lansing Switch Road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257524> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "FM 449 near Franklin Road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1257525> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple county roads across Harrison County were flooded and closed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1258633> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain during the night of April 25th resulted in flooding of most of the access road near McCormick Road and I-27. It remained covered in water into the next morning and was barely passable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1258637> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain occurred on the night of April 25th. There was strong evidence that Spring Creek flooded Shady Lake Drive to the point where the road was impassable and water still remained over the road the following morning." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1260977> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report was received from the public via MPING that flash flooding of streets/roads was occurring near Knott. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar. No damage was reported." .

