<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1261985> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Facebook report of CR 326 and CR 322 both flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262193> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "High water covered portions of FM 2710, with several cars stranded in the floodwaters." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262195> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "CR 472 was flooded near FM 463." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262286> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple roads were flooded in Longview." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262291> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Portions of Pearl Street was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262404> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A flash flood was reported by Pecos County Emergency Management. Water appeared to be several feet over the road based on the report. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262408> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "US Highway 285 at Nineteen Draw is flooded over, and the road may be starting to wash out. The road is likely to be closed through the night. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar and based on the reported severity of the flooding. The cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1262412> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Pecos County Emergency Manager reported that 3 high water rescues were taking place 4  miles south of I-10 along RM 2023. Up to 4 ft of water was reported to be across the road. The total time interval during which the flood occurred is estimated from radar and estimated runoff time. The cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1263785> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was 5-6 feet of water over FM 334 near Ox Ranch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264251> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding of a low water crossing on Cypress Ln. at Black House Creek in Cedar Park." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264254> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing McNeil Dr. at Mopac in Wells Branch." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264258> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing CR 349 at Opossum Creek east of Granger." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264280> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding in Eagle Pass. There was water in homes and high water vehicle rescues. One vehicle was swept into a canal near Roosevelt St. and Austin St. The car became lodged under a bridge at Wilson St. The lone occupant, an 18 year old male, was found deceased in the Rio Grande River, just south of International Bridge II." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264281> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding in Eagle Pass. El Indio Highway was flooded near Memo Robinson Dr." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264540> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Low water crossings on Old Spicewood Rd. along Bull Creek were flooded in northern Austin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264549> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing a few low water crossings in northwestern Bexar County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264552> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding closing several low water crossings in north-central San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264555> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There were multiple high water rescues in central and northern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264617> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood.org reported  several low water crossings closed in northwestern Bexar County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264618> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood.org reported several low water crossings in northern and central Bexar County were flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264619> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The exit from northbound Hwy 281 to Hwy 46 was closed for around 50 minutes due to water over the road. There were multiple rescues of people stuck in vehicles in the water." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264620> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was a water rescue on Blanco Rd. near Cibolo Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264624> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The San Antonio Fire Department rescued a driver from their car in flood water on W. Commerce St. at Leon Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1264683> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "SPID frontage road near Ennis Joslin Road closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265159> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A car was stranded in high water near the intersection of Loop 323 and Highway 271." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265161> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several high water rescues were needed for stranded motorists under the railroad overpasses in Longview, including Green Street and Nelson Street, Green Street and Cotton Street, and High Street and Cotton Street. In addition, several low lying areas across the city were flooded as well." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265163> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Highway 135 north of the traffic circle in Kilgore was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265165> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The inside lane of Highway 110 (Troup Highway) was flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265166> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The exit from northbound Hwy 281 to Hwy 46 was closed for around 20 minutes with water over the road. There were water rescues of multiple people stuck in vehicles." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265170> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was a swift water rescue on the I-35 feeder road near Buttermilk Branch in northern Austin." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265173> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Two vehicles were stranded in water on Steck Ave. near MOPAC in northern Austin. The occupants of these vehicles had to be rescued." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265177> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding occurred across the city of  Austin with 6 water rescues reported, some  of which included vehicles. On the 2200  Block of Hancock Drive near the Yarborough  Branch of the Austin Public Library, an unhoused  individual was swept away when Hancock Creek flooded. The body of the person was recovered downstream." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265186> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Widespread flooding was reported across Denton with I-35W closed and diverted to I-35E." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265274> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There were multiple stranded vehicles and high water rescues reported across San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265276> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Several low water crossings were closed over northeastern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265277> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There were stranded vehicle and water rescue along Old  O'Connor Road in northeastern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1265278> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The lower deck of I-10 at Culebra Rd. was flooded in San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266223> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Traffic cameras showed road closure due to high water along frontage roads along I-10 E at Jensen. Broadcast media also reported submerged cars in the underpass along Navigation Blvd." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266315> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "AN emergency manager reported local street flooding at FM 517 at IH45, on FM 517 just west of the intersection at IH45." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266341> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A storm chaser shared a video on social media showing the aftermath of heavy rains in Blessing Texas. A large area of standing water can be seen over one property. Additional videos showed debris over the roadway along FM 1862 from flooding. Shallow water was still flowing over the roadway several hours after the event concluded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266362> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Storm chaser shared video on social media showing ponding on I-69 frontage road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266381> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A storm chaser shared a video on social media showing the aftermath of heavy rains in Blessing Texas. A large area of standing water can be seen over one property. Additional videos showed debris over the roadway along FM 1862 from flooding. Shallow water was still flowing over the roadway several hours after the event concluded, with surrounding areas still inundated well after the rains ended." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266388> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Minor flooding occurred over portions of FM 363." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266390> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A gage reported Pin Oak Creek was out of its banks near Kirbyville. Multiple roads near Buna also had minor flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266391> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The stream gage reported Big Cow Creek exceeded bankfull." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1266790> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported multiple roads in Edna covered in floodwaters from heavy rain. A few vehicles were reported as stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267012> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report was received from the public via mPING of street flooding on the west side of Odessa. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar. No reports of damage were received." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267014> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report was received from the public via mPING of street flooding just west of Notrees. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar. No reports of damage were received." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267015> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report from the public was received via mPING of street flooding on the north side of Lamesa. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar. No reports of damage were received." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267017> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report was received from the public via mPING of street flooding southwest of O'Donnell near/along US 87. The time of occurrence is estimated from radar. No reports of damage were received." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267464> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The public posted pictures on social media showing streets flooded and yards flooded in Menard." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267466> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public report of streets flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267467> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported streets flooded and yards flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267469> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An NWS employee reported flooding on a roadway, with water flowing across the road. In addition, extensive flooding was reported across the city of San Angelo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1267505> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported flooding in yard." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1268116> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The emergency manager reported about 3 to 4 inches of rain. In Palestine, water had been running over the road near 325 Spring Street, and cars were stalled in water near 936 W Oak." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1268235> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Fast moving flood waters covered County Road J just off HWY 60. Water was at least 6 to 8 inches deep." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1269377> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several inches of runoff over FM 1776 with at least 10 low water crossings between  Coyanosa and US 285. Time is estimated based on radar and reports. The property cost damage is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1269378> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding up to 1 foot deep at times over I-10 at mile marker 171. The duration is estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1269380> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report from mPING was received of flash flooding. This report was likely a result of water across low water crossings along the road in and out of the Buffalo Trail Scout Ranch. Duration is an estimation." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1269387> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Pecos County Emergency Manager reported approximately one foot of water over Highway  385 at Six Shooter Draw. Duration is estimated from radar and reports." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1269401> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Five vehicles were reported stalled in high water due to flash flooding across various locations in Midland. The duration of these incidents is an estimation. The property damage cost is an estimation." .

