<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271379> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported water flowing over FM 1311 just inside the McCulloch County line near Calf Creek, causing the road to be impassable." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271384> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An emergency manager reported 6 to 8 feet of water flowing over FM 2092, at the Five Mile Crossing, 5 miles east of Menard. The road was closed due to flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271442> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public report of flood waters over FM 605 and FM 707 on social media. Some portions of the road had flood water depth around 2 feet. Estimated time of peak flooding based on radar data." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271444> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public report of street flooding." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271808> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain occurred in Palo Duro Canyon, which resulted in flash flooding. The flooding closed a portion of the main road going through the canyon." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271810> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Standing water occurred in the outer lanes of US 87 in Canyon." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271842> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Both directions of I-40 at Hope Road were  closed due to water over the roadway.  Traffic was being detoured to the frontage  road." .

