<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271948> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The Banta Branch of the Pedernales River was out of its banks southwest of Harper." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271960> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. RM 152 and RM 2323 were closed at some of the tributaries to the Llano River east and southeast of Castell." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271988> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Public reported water flowing across Toe Nail Trail in Christoval due to heavy rainfall." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271993> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Bexarflood.org showed several low water crossings closed in northwestern Bexar County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1271994> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A trained spotter reported high water on the roads beginning to flood vehicles in  northwest portions of Abilene, with additional reports of flash flooding around the rest of Abilene." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272201> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported in Mount Pleasant via Mping." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272208> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The San Antonio Fire Department completed three high water rescues from some of 18 flooded low water crossings in northwest and north-central San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272213> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported with water covering the road on Highway 80 between Marshall and Hallsville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272215> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported across the highway with a high water rescue that occurred." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272217> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported in downtown Tyler." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272222> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Flash flooding reported with County Road 4211 closed due to water over the road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272279> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Training of thunderstorms with intense rainfall rates produced a swath of 3-8 inches of rain in San Antonio. A vehicle was swept into Leon Creek near Callaghan Rd. and Hwy 90 and the driver died. The vehicle was discovered on June 14th." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272284> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Mud Creek overflowed near the Saddle Mountain subdivision in the Stone Oak area of San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272286> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Olmos Creek overflowed in northern San Antonio." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272287> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. The Comal County Sheriff reported several low water crossings flooded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272290> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. A normally dry creek overflowed in Garden Ridge." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272294> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. The normally dry Walnut Branch overflowed northeast of McQueeney." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272295> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Bexarflood.org reported 29 low water crossings flooded in northern Bexar County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272297> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Multiple low water crossings were reported closed around Wimberley." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272298> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. There was a news report of nine homes flooded along Shin Oak Dr. in Live Oak." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272299> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. Cottonwood Creek flooded a low water crossing on Old Bastrop Hwy near Capistrano Dr." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272305> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Training of thunderstorms with intense rainfall rates produced a swath of 3-8 inches of rain across San Antonio. A non-vehicle related fatality was reported near Wurzbach Pkwy and Salado Creek. The body was discovered on June 14th. The exact location of where this person went into the water is not known." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272317> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain leading to flash flooding. York Creek overflowed closing York Creek Rd. west of Zorn." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272324> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Training of thunderstorms with intense rainfall rates produced a swath of 3-8 inches of rain across San Antonio. Several vehicles were swept off the Loop 410 access road into Beitel Creek. There were 11 fatalities in this creek and the surrounding area. Ten people were rescued from the water, and two others were able to get to safety on their own. Damage from the flooding totaled $23 million across Bexar County." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272329> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. One of our broadcast partners showed a photo of cars submerged on the main lanes of southbound I-35 at FM 3009." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272336> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The occupants of a vehicle were rescued after they were swept off the road on CR 2615 near CR 372 in the vicinity of the Medina River north of Rio Medina." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272339> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The occupants of a vehicle were rescued after they were swept off the road on CR 381 in the vicinity of San Geronimo Creek northeast of Rio Medina." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272340> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was a high water rescue on I-35 near the Windcrest Business Park along Walzem Creek." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272344> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. The Emergency Manager reported flooding along FM 2790 between the South Wind Subdivision and Luckey Rd. east of Lytle. There were multiple water rescues." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272350> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Thunderstorms produced heavy rain that led to flash flooding. There was water over Hwy 119 along with other low water crossings flooded near Smith Creek south of Yorktown." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272664> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported 21 vehicles stalled in high water due to flash flooding across various portions of Midland, TX. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. The total cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272665> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management reported many evacuations of campgrounds in the Big Bend area due to flash flooding. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damages were reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272666> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Extremely heavy rain around Marfa and Fort Davis produced widespread street flooding. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272667> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management in Alpine reported one home inundated by flooding due to heavy  rainfall and numerous road closures by local authorities. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. The total cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272668> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A Texas Parks and Wildlife Park Ranger reported high water over FM 170 East at Terneros  Creek. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272669> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency Management reported high water due to flash flooding impacting Highway 87 in southeastern Dawson County. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272670> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Park rangers at the Big Bend reported flood water rushing through Long Draw Creek over FM 170. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272671> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement reported road closed due to down powerlines and flooding on FM 57 between U.S. Highway 180 and U.S. Highway 83." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272672> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple road closures were reported across Dawson County due to flooded roadways. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272674> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A storm chaser reported street flooding in Albany. Time estimated from radar." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272679> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "The Drive Texas website indicated water was covering the roadway of the Business I-20  north service road near East Loop 338. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. No damage was reported." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272721> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A total of 12 water rescues were reported throughout the city of Odessa. The time of occurrence is estimated by radar. The cost of damages is also estimated." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272954> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rain produced an estimated 6 to 12 inches of fast flowing water on couple of  residential streets in the northwest part of Amarillo." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272955> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "An estimated three to four feet of fast flowing water occurred in a normally dry creek bed." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1272960> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Heavy rainfall brought flooding along Williams Street. At least an inch of water entered a couple of homes in the neighborhood." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1273200> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "A report from mPING indicated street/road flooding; street/road closed; and vehicles stranded." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1273202> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several roads were flooded and closed across  Rowlett, including Princeton Rd at Coventry Dr, Rowlett Rd at Miller Rd with two stranded vehicles, Hwy 66 at Sprouts Dr with three stranded vehicles, and Rowlett Rd at Locust St with five vehicles stranded. A member of the public also reported that five homes were flooded with about one foot deep of water on Scott Drive." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1273203> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Broadcast media reported that a section of I-35 was flooded and impassable in Lewisville." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1273834> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Water covered the road near 23rd and 4th Street. Road was passable but up to 4 inches  deep on sides of road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1274497> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Emergency management reported that several roads sustained flood damage to bridges and culverts, or had areas of the roadway washed away, including County Roads 3715, 1500, 1507, 3822, 3918, 1113 near the city of Athens, and FM 316 near the city of Athens." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1274500> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads were reported flooded and closed across Garland including Campbell Road, Castle Drive and Naaman School Road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1275150> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Report from mPING.  Street/road flooding east of Montana Vista also confirmed by social media." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1275171> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Trained spotter reported flash flooding along Dyer near US 54.  Social media showed a flooded AutoZone parking lot." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1275226> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Social media post in the area showing multiple spots of standing and flowing water on roadways south of the airport." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1275504> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Minor roadway flooding along McNeil Avenue. The report was relayed through Spotter Network. The location and event time are approximate." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1275988> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous reports were received of flash flooding within the city of Lubbock from law enforcement and members of the public. An intense thunderstorm slowly moved from southeast to northwest across the city of Lubbock producing heavy rainfall. Texas Tech University West Texas mesonet sites in the city of Lubbock recorded over an inch of rainfall in less than 20 minutes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1275989> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous reports were received of flash flooding within the city of Lubbock from law enforcement and members of the public. An intense thunderstorm slowly moved from southeast to northwest across the city of Lubbock producing heavy rainfall. Texas Tech University West Texas mesonet sites in the city of Lubbock recorded over an inch of rainfall in less than 20 minutes." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1276422> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple reports of minor street flooding were received from Beaumont." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1276423> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Several roads were impassable in Beaumont including the feeder along Hwy 69, Cedar, the intersection of College and MLK, the underpass in Downtown Beaumont, Orleans, and the feeder of I-10 near Babe Zaharias." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1276455> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Multiple streets were flooded in Beaumont with one water level gage reported water just under 2 feet over the roadway near downtown." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1276457> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Numerous streets flooded in Beaumont with cars stalled on North 11th and on the I-10 service road." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1276459> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Washington Blvd near MLK in Downtown Beaumont became impassable. The Crocket Street underpass was also filled to the top." .

<http://floodkg.org/event/noaa/1278128> <http://floodkg.org/hasNarrative> "Law enforcement, trained spotters and the public reported several roads across Denton were flooded. A trained spotter reported that South Carroll Avenue, one half mile south of US 380, was impassable due to flooding with stalled vehicles." .

